state\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[279]:=",
 CellID->237269248,ExpressionUUID->"45b5dbb0-b576-45eb-734a-d2fa3c032f31"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ce9c8c0-fe52-3cd7-7496-e1adfbe4863d"],
 " climbs from zero to one: the maximally mixed state is driven to a pure \
state by its own record. This is measurement-based feedback control, the \
basis of feedback cooling and qubit stabilization."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1574480490,ExpressionUUID->"4c678cac-5cc4-b18e-741c-25f6557603d4"],

Cell["\<\
The loop has a causal chain worth seeing whole: the noisy record drives a \
control command, which drives the state's response. That same run already \
carries both, so take seed 2 and read its per-step command against its \
response:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1044501402,ExpressionUUID->"0528a095-4bdb-63f8-2cd7-39df6e6e31c2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"feedRun", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"steer", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[280]:=",
 CellID->1803296954,ExpressionUUID->"1a78d2a2-b26e-4f45-4a07-cb0fc71b15af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now visualize the loop in time, two panels side by side: the feedback \
rotation the raw record commands at each step, a noise band, and the state's \
response ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "316f19e5-f7db-2937-6714-90ce826e781d"],
 " climbing to the target:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1178089277,ExpressionUUID->"3daec99f-8291-5f2c-6b55-e0d937242276"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"track", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", ";;"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"feedRun", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"2", " ", ";;"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
       "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "Medium"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<feedback rotation\>\""}], 
        "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
      "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
       " ", "\"\<the command the raw record drives\>\""}]}], "]"}], ",", 
    " ", "\"\<  \>\"", ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"track", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", ";;"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
             RowBox[{"#", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"feedRun", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", ";;"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "Medium"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Sigma]x\[RightAngleBracket]\>\""}], 
        "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
      "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<the response it produces\>\""}]}], 
     "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[281]:=",
 CellID->499442545,ExpressionUUID->"5dea9ab6-68b8-c529-0be9-13f00932ac73"],

Cell["\<\
Command to response, left to right: the loop reads the noisy record as a \
rotation, a noise band, and the rotations walk the state smoothly to the \
target.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1977375848,ExpressionUUID->"030af18e-b5e5-d347-3109-e8ebc391a1ad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "But a real loop never has a perfect detector, and inefficiency caps how \
pure the steered state can get. The Wiseman-Milburn feedback master equation \
carries an efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "405f2726-590a-86f0-7064-be8058bcecda"],
 " that adds an irreducible feedback-noise term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"1", "-", 
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "\|01d49f", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "385fe069-90bd-43ce-6864-fa3321481114"],
 "; solve its steady state against ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "709f1246-ab2e-00b9-20a4-9423cedb5283"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1792186819,ExpressionUUID->"50a39cef-8bd0-9934-0050-15c92e6ae81e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"steadyXeff", "[", "\[Eta]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
     RowBox[{"First", "@", 
      RowBox[{"stationary", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"0", " ", "id2"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "Gfb", "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"Z", " ", "-", " ", 
             RowBox[{"I", " ", "Y"}]}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "\[Eta]"}], ")"}], "/", "\[Eta]"}], 
            "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "Gfb", "]"}], " ", "Y"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
     "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"etasFb", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0.3", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0.05"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"etasFb", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"steadyXeff", " ", "/@", " ", "etasFb"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotMarkers", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
     RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "460"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<detection efficiency \[Eta]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<steady \
\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Sigma]x\[RightAngleBracket]\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<a leaky detector cannot fully purify: feedback noise sets the \
floor\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[282]:=",
 CellID->883014421,ExpressionUUID->"6eea4472-a755-a6aa-16ea-5e3fd2e10cf0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Steady ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d344668-2780-d87f-44cc-5832523aab45"],
 " climbs to one only as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ae7ede6-d60d-06a2-2a9c-04c3e3b86c88"],
 "; a lossy detector leaves the loop feeding its own missing information back \
as noise, and the target is reached only in part. Perfect stabilization needs \
a perfect record, the same efficiency limit that capped the feedback \
cooling."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1335019792,ExpressionUUID->"71444f73-786e-4642-277c-673d791b2ca8"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Part Six: Settling Warm, Purifying Fast, Cooling Cold", "Section",
 CellID->162990234,ExpressionUUID->"74f6de95-8032-4c15-1c8d-d7df31c7177f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Thermalization to a Bath", "Subsection",
 CellID->1864261496,ExpressionUUID->"389004b5-9a2c-3ef3-68af-9dff1fde84d9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The problem.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A warm bath both takes and gives energy, settling a system at its own \
temperature. For an oscillator,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->875071895,ExpressionUUID->"2d697f6b-3d93-338c-5b17-7735b42781d6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "."], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]}], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", "1"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox["1", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"\[Beta]", "\[Omega]"}], "TI"]], "-", "1"}]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1252034050,ExpressionUUID->"20a70809-2e49-b141-505c-a2534bfd03ab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where the down-rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7723626c-4939-a85b-1ed0-843668cdfaa1"],
 " beats the up-rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6663ba53-1d85-6946-0e10-3c1d94303bac"],
 " by exactly the Boltzmann factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"\[Beta]", "\[Omega]"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2a52a343-e04e-4391-5a61-3b2c91fb11fb"],
 ". This ",
 StyleBox["detailed balance", "TI"],
 " forces the steady state to the thermal distribution ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["ss",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[Proportional]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48a3001a-e719-cbe1-7850-9a4792ad99cb"],
 " with mean occupation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31ebe54c-d1b5-c56d-67e8-fd29e041afb7"],
 ". Settle a cold and a hot start and confirm both land on the thermal \
distribution."
}], "Text",
 CellID->41937841,ExpressionUUID->"1dddb0f1-9068-854b-4be2-29bb2102ef91"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A warm bath both absorbs and emits, settling a system at its temperature. \
Model it as two dissipators: decay ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4eea920a-da78-9b5c-76e9-1457dff2e9a6"],
 " at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f55f164-a56a-0bbf-256a-e941cc1f5985"],
 " and excitation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66a2faf2-58b3-40d9-0e51-f3bc59461223"],
 " at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1685e188-3be3-a90f-3eba-f8d2bd97f855"],
 ". Set the cutoff, the ladder, the bath occupation and its rate:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1124512868,ExpressionUUID->"1a321877-2c7f-2cce-4bc1-9231450a7614"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"topTh", " ", "=", " ", "24"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"annihilation", "[", "topTh", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"count", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"creation", "[", "topTh", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "a"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"nT", " ", "=", " ", "1.2"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]th", " ", "=", " ", "0.5"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[285]:=",
 CellID->225942279,ExpressionUUID->"4421f40f-2283-9b1b-6dde-ee695737e661"],

Cell["\<\
The two channels, decay and excitation, with their thermal weights:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->15750989,ExpressionUUID->"612520b5-066b-562d-10da-b9ffb31e3d77"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"fall", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]th", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"nT", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", "a"}]}], ";", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{"climb", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]th", " ", "nT"}], "]"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"creation", "[", "topTh", "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[286]:=",
 CellID->20337601,ExpressionUUID->"4b20a0de-bf05-fd95-7adf-39983ab1c7ff"],

Cell["The mean occupation of a state:", "Text",
 CellID->127439427,ExpressionUUID->"4a88aa2f-b14b-d52b-7ab7-4388c0ffbc71"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"units", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{"expectation", "[", 
     RowBox[{"count", ",", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[287]:=",
 CellID->1378080400,ExpressionUUID->"57b69005-8bc5-b0fd-7d4d-0a6f2e7102c7"],

Cell["Settle a cold (vacuum) and a hot start:", "Text",
 CellID->880029775,ExpressionUUID->"72f2455d-c49b-2bf1-2282-5d06ed2e79db"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"fromCold", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"evolveODE", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"0", " ", 
      RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "topTh", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"fall", ",", " ", "climb"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", 
      RowBox[{"coherentState", "[", 
       RowBox[{"topTh", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "16."}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"fromHot", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"evolveODE", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"0", " ", 
      RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "topTh", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"fall", ",", " ", "climb"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", 
      RowBox[{"UnitVector", "[", 
       RowBox[{"topTh", ",", " ", "9"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "16."}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[288]:=",
 CellID->1216675886,ExpressionUUID->"77416ebe-6e08-cf7c-1d7e-87f80ba29246"],

Cell["\<\
Read as a dynamical law, this equation has three consequences worth drawing \
out one at a time, each sharper than the one before.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->764992932,ExpressionUUID->"18599260-685f-792c-4866-144a09ea4876"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first is a ",
 StyleBox["single attractor",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": the evolution forgets the initial state, so every start relaxes to the \
same steady state. Test that from opposite extremes, the cold vacuum and the \
hot ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32a0fa91-0c97-025a-625f-f3dba52250a0"],
 " state, by reading their late mean occupations against ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d4f6d29-8280-add7-4b74-8573373af73d"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->746121340,ExpressionUUID->"7d1d4b7f-00e8-6ae3-2b23-6339b09d38c9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"units", "[", 
    RowBox[{"fromCold", "[", "16.", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"units", "[", 
    RowBox[{"fromHot", "[", "16.", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "nT"}], 
  "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[290]:=",
 CellID->1139255012,ExpressionUUID->"3b093cc2-afd1-7ed1-6936-b5afca64443b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both land on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023dde7a-8e23-336a-33c2-d0242bd781b0"],
 ". Watch them get there, the cold climbing and the hot relaxing until they \
meet:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->965302876,ExpressionUUID->"40fb5a43-fbb5-27db-7099-5c2cfe418d21"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "16", ",", " ", "0.05"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"units", "[", 
           RowBox[{"fromCold", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "16", ",", " ", "0.05"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], 
      "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "16", ",", " ", "0.05"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"units", "[", 
           RowBox[{"fromHot", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "16", ",", " ", "0.05"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], 
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nT"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"16", ",", " ", "nT"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<from cold\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<from hot\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<warm equilibrium\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<mean occupation\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<both starts reach the thermal mean\>\""}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[291]:=",
 CellID->1302650277,ExpressionUUID->"2425f502-e1b1-2adc-4dda-ed6f90447826"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "They settle on the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "212476b8-b137-7f4a-50dc-6fe5c0c24590"],
 " from opposite sides: the bath drains the hot oscillator and feeds the cold \
one, so wherever the state began, it ends where decay and excitation balance. \
This two-way traffic is what makes the attractor unique; the pure-dephasing \
bath of Part One, which only froze populations, left a whole line of steady \
states instead."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1688685886,ExpressionUUID->"3db10d53-0e34-1357-6b4e-a51dabc161bd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the infinite oscillator model, the mean occupation follows an exact \
closed path. Tracing the master equation against ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e4bd926-69e3-4ee0-6648-d0800f9614ca"],
 " gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57d10123-a1d4-e454-7dee-988cd066cebe"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27645c90-4345-b83d-4d1c-55da76f10b07"],
 ". The finite-cutoff simulation should approach that law; check the cold \
start (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "245848e5-b774-8ea9-4c78-61cec206d4f3"],
 "):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->632063892,ExpressionUUID->"0581f938-6b6a-81e3-33be-f1620e1cd3c9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"units", "[", 
       RowBox[{"fromCold", "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"nT", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "\[Gamma]th"}], " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}],
     ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "16", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[292]:=",
 CellID->1331054704,ExpressionUUID->"7e58b706-7f01-9af1-2667-2f607ab5e8db"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The reported nonzero residual is the combined cutoff and ODE error; \
increasing the dimension and tightening solver tolerances reduce it. In the \
untruncated law one relaxation rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b1945ac-ce61-156f-3927-5c09eb147fb5"],
 " carries the mean from its start to the bath value. The first field moment \
obeys the same kind of law but half as fast and while rotating, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d8aaa59-0983-f6a5-6b89-4c03a837dc8f"],
 "; the code sets ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f61b3a8-54be-2aae-151e-2af25d4b78f4"],
 ", so no rotation is drawn here: the frequency appears in coherence rather \
than number populations."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1024214867,ExpressionUUID->"334edda2-111d-1275-6175-d40ca0a8615f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The second consequence is stronger: the equation fixes ",
 StyleBox["the whole state",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", not just its mean. A mean is weak evidence, since a coherent, a squeezed, \
and a thermal state can all share the occupation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "705f43d3-b8fa-6681-2065-5a9d388f4ceb"],
 ". So build the settled populations and the geometric thermal shape ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e6e22f7-e70d-ed4b-3615-bbb092b9b791"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f79e66b-a47f-c7f6-5506-f834cd0baddc"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->509901081,ExpressionUUID->"26eacd00-7450-3870-4ee9-e56a7dea8b5a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"pops", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Diagonal", "[", 
      RowBox[{"fromCold", "[", "16.", "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{";;", " ", "8"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"warmShape", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"ratio", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"nT", "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"nT", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "ratio"}], ")"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"ratio", "^", 
       RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "7"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[293]:=",
 CellID->1957271700,ExpressionUUID->"0a9819e1-44ec-6fcb-3aa7-90cb6c993511"],

Cell["Read the largest gap between them:", "Text",
 CellID->935291515,ExpressionUUID->"2241f5e7-2cd3-435b-527e-ecc1456611a1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{"pops", " ", "-", " ", "warmShape"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[295]:=",
 CellID->2045201311,ExpressionUUID->"2d2e5055-b89d-3ae5-54d6-4a1f392988cf"],

Cell["\<\
They agree to a fraction of a percent. Level by level, the settled \
populations sit on the thermal bars rung for rung:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->129431700,ExpressionUUID->"60242f61-d35b-0cea-11db-c74ae6ee5630"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"BarChart", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "@", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"pops", ",", " ", "warmShape"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ChartLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<settled\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<thermal\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"ChartLabels", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "7"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "None"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Fock level\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<probability\>\""}], "}"}]}],
    ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<the settled distribution is thermal\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[296]:=",
 CellID->359040978,ExpressionUUID->"6b2a7c99-762e-0564-192a-75c303db6c4e"],

Cell["\<\
The attractor is a complete density matrix; reaching the thermal mean was \
only its shadow.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1429785775,ExpressionUUID->"15f5c2c8-4d3f-e85b-438a-db9264cbbaa1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The third consequence is the deepest, the point where a dynamical equation \
reproduces equilibrium statistical mechanics. Stationarity alone forces the \
population ratio on adjacent rungs to equal the ratio of the two rates, \
excitation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14c9f408-7194-4cc4-3cf6-ee520021162e"],
 " over decay ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38fb8547-75f1-44dc-6898-1d2103842e26"],
 ", and that flux balance is mere bookkeeping. The physics is that the ratio \
is not free: through ",
 StyleBox["detailed balance",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " the bath locks the downward rate above the upward one by exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"\[Beta]", "\[Omega]"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71ac5ef3-5fe8-d867-2754-57bd5982ab4d"],
 ", its own thermal signature, so an oscillator with no temperature of its \
own is driven into the Boltzmann distribution at the bath's temperature. The \
canonical ensemble is derived here, not assumed:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1008132517,ExpressionUUID->"29854b4c-a654-c8a2-5fbb-6329d3e69a88"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]th", " ", "nT"}], ")"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]th", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"nT", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"nT", "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"nT", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[297]:=",
 CellID->764580650,ExpressionUUID->"59c17136-c551-666f-0fff-6973ece44cb5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two are equal, both ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "345db6df-ede1-7415-5c62-2f988b945f7f"],
 ". The settled state shows the same thing directly: a geometric distribution \
is a straight line on a log axis, its constant slope the Boltzmann factor. \
Plot the settled populations against the thermal shape:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->302184118,ExpressionUUID->"23d8e320-2d42-669a-51e7-fa8a44f74ce0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"fock", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ListLogPlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"fock", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"pops", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{";;", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Length", "@", "fock"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], 
       ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"fock", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"warmShape", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{";;", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Length", "@", "fock"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
        "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Joined", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotMarkers", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"Automatic", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<settled\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<thermal\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FrameTicks", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"fock", ",", " ", "Automatic"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"fock", ",", " ", "Automatic"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Fock level n\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<population (log)\>\""}],
        "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
     "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<geometric tail: a straight line on a log axis\>\""}]}], 
    "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[298]:=",
 CellID->1619716671,ExpressionUUID->"296ab46d-a3f4-f13b-5f69-2e36d586c001"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The settled populations fall on a straight line, parallel to the thermal \
one and with the same constant slope: every rung is less likely than the one \
below by the bath's Boltzmann factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cac3d4d-2028-a76d-1453-b51751c20db7"],
 ", the visible fingerprint of detailed balance. The ratio of rates in the \
equation has become the slope of the ladder in the state. Damping and \
thermalization are then one process: decay ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f515ffd-22dc-f8c8-256f-56a7576eca12"],
 " and excitation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36fe791f-fced-9eb8-5e86-7158f499e482"],
 " are the same bath, and the ground-state relaxation of the earlier examples \
is its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76a256fd-37ed-da8a-1e52-4fa74199a8d0"],
 " corner, an oscillator settling to its bath temperature with its whole \
distribution fixed by two rates."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1797210921,ExpressionUUID->"6deb6a83-c2a1-684f-1be8-83ecf7543a95"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Rapid Purification by Feedback", "Subsection",
 CellID->454532135,ExpressionUUID->"789236d2-9f43-12ba-28a1-af9c1af66080"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The problem.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Continuously watching an observable extracts information and sharpens the \
state toward one of its eigenstates, so a monitored qubit purifies with time. \
Measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "+", 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "383adb7b-ef12-e6f5-69d9-d3248aa4ccdf"],
 " at strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d2f2d89-c57c-c791-74d4-c4d2ec0eadfb"],
 " with no drive (the leak is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0be1af94-d211-8aa3-399e-46d1e7a5d889"],
 "), a stationary axis tilted by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20c93ef5-aaf5-6d2e-50f6-b7bece803474"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d278640-9b14-0749-54dc-182a1ea16d93"],
 "; the conditioned state obeys the same measurement equation as the \
localization example, now along that tilted axis,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->960455850,ExpressionUUID->"27508344-1169-d276-4d6f-1b2ea01da15c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "=", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "+", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["c", "TI"]], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], "-", "2", 
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["c", "TI"]]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["W", "TI"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->588212915,ExpressionUUID->"52bd9efb-5696-d8d3-0242-17a56320aa39"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Watch it happen before dissecting the rate: fix one tilted axis, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "=", "0.7"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "59d784c6-d1d1-3822-0fec-1da3e0658b08"],
 ", measure it at unit strength on the maximally mixed state, and follow the \
purity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0af74c3d-c5cb-eb2b-3a8d-6666ec7fb671"],
 " of five conditioned runs."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1438862008,ExpressionUUID->"18e44c83-1c1f-43b5-489c-65ed95aa119f"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mAxis", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "0.7", "]"}], " ", "X"}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "0.7", "]"}], " ", "Z"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"purities", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"purity", " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"id2", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"0", " ", "id2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "mAxis", "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "0.01", ",", " ", "1.5", ",", " ", 
         "k"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"0.01", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Length", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], 
          "]"}]}], ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    "purities"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<purity\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"Automatic", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0.4", ",", " ", "1.02"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", "Thick"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<monitoring purifies every conditioned run\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[299]:=",
 CellID->1022895307,ExpressionUUID->"6026f33f-0f19-e769-11dd-eb79aaadcdb3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All five runs climb from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox["1", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06331a5a-5e36-eeb4-2fc0-9c045bc0b49e"],
 " toward ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23db06c9-5192-a0c1-51f8-9f936024f22b"],
 ": monitoring alone has turned the maximally mixed qubit nearly pure, the \
raw content of \"purifies with time.\" Each climb is jagged because these are \
",
 StyleBox["conditioned", "TI"],
 " histories, each driven by its own record's noise; averaging the \
conditioned states over many records leaves the qubit fixed at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox["1", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7de6255b-dc63-5143-2b9d-bd04d51623a9"],
 ", since the maximally mixed state is a steady state of the unconditional \
evolution. Purification is a fact about each watched trajectory, not the \
record-blind average. Measuring one stationary axis, held put for the whole \
run, is the unsteered case; the steered strategy below re-aims the axis each \
step instead."
}], "Text",
 CellID->424225543,ExpressionUUID->"6e05cf72-a918-1ba6-163a-e73fc8ad698c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How fast it purifies depends on where the state sits relative to that axis, \
an angle that itself moves: let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27233357-6f43-6494-4ed0-ab110af64efe"],
 " be the instantaneous angle between the Bloch vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5de364a1-4a4c-e5c4-0b91-7d0b6ffecf2e"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "691f1a66-023d-d875-1f24-9c40b7c9ab5f"],
 ". (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "338a64d0-666f-51f5-618a-7d9a131a23df"],
 " is not ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "457416e7-7538-701a-730b-8fc17ccd4360"],
 ": ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48945f4c-b90a-f7cd-78ac-571638bcdd17"],
 " fixes where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "138a5a7b-a86c-a778-418a-5c24c91e0a42"],
 " points and stays constant, while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "508ec8d0-0dfb-c87e-00b5-e19aab8f9b44"],
 " measures where the state sits relative to it and moves with the record.) \
Writing the impurity as the random variable ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        SubscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2a8e75db-4196-2992-5ab6-6c8570237bf8"],
 ", It\[OHat]'s rule turns the measurement equation above into a full \
stochastic increment,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1694748468,ExpressionUUID->"10b44722-1d8a-a843-404c-5e8c943cfaa9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "-", "4", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["sin",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "+", "2", 
     SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["cos",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[ThickSpace]", "-", "\[ThickSpace]", "4", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], 
    SqrtBox[
     RowBox[{"1", "-", "2", 
      SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->377500653,ExpressionUUID->"376a42de-a72c-dab7-5d6a-5b9bd2dea89d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The noise carries the factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e950789-7bdf-2365-46aa-9ed37e6b8e4f"],
 ", and that factor is the whole story. If feedback holds the axis ",
 StyleBox["perpendicular", "TI"],
 " to the Bloch vector, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66a9921e-bad7-8e47-0e56-14583f63d4ad"],
 ", the noise coefficient vanishes and the impurity is deterministic for ",
 StyleBox["every", "TI"],
 " record, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "-", "4", 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "17d2ef91-60a0-4e89-3de1-06db115514d3"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", "0"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "4", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fb9f494-3700-dcc2-2546-edde42baa628"],
 ": the fast case. If instead the axis lies ",
 StyleBox["along", "TI"],
 " the Bloch vector, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43fac4e6-e09d-fa6e-7199-ddc39129c8b4"],
 ", the noise is maximal and the impurity keeps fluctuating,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->827200276,ExpressionUUID->"2968eab2-ef34-759a-5f17-03ff8ac15fe0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "-", "8", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "-", "4", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], 
    SqrtBox[
     RowBox[{"1", "-", "2", 
      SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->19958409,ExpressionUUID->"5d87f42e-d652-8147-0bbc-ed8be3e4d3ad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with no deterministic pathwise solution; only its ensemble mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "\|01d53c", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "556a1f76-4155-b78b-0369-973070e11dd1"],
 " can be tracked, through the nonclosed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "."], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "-", "8", 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\|01d53c", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ae11f47-bcab-5fd1-1a9e-9721355e253b"],
 ". A stationary measurement axis lets the state drift into alignment (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14be3adf-0864-81d7-3c45-b399a916d33d"],
 "), where it learns slowly and stochastically: the back-action (the \
measurement's kick back on the state) pulls the Bloch vector toward whatever \
axis is measured, so an axis that never moves is one the state keeps falling \
into. Holding ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fc6e9dd-9955-7f76-15fd-008718e0425c"],
 " therefore takes constant re-aiming, and that re-aiming is the feedback: it \
keeps the axis perpendicular to the moving state and with it the fast, \
deterministic rate. Because the feedback resets the axis to perpendicular \
only at discrete steps, the state drifts off ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "18ddee5b-7ce8-2fa7-48e2-0005749d758d"],
 " within each step, and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1012f954-cdfa-9bde-4021-f111eb8ce924"],
 " noise term in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14c14cd5-eb1e-28e1-3cff-659e8eab7acb"],
 " no longer cancels exactly; the residue is a record-dependent path spread \
that vanishes as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c226993-d8a3-5fdb-35d1-80dcd9562521"],
 ". This is ",
 ButtonBox["Jacobs' rapid-purification protocol",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0301056"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2075932104,ExpressionUUID->"50d2e924-c37a-d2d3-00e1-0081f60ca039"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "There is a catch in what \"fast\" means. Keeping the measurement \
perpendicular maximizes the ",
 StyleBox["mean purity at a fixed time", "TI"],
 ", yet it ",
 StyleBox["lengthens", "TI"],
 " the mean time to reach a chosen purity, because its determinism forbids \
the lucky fast runs an aligned measurement occasionally enjoys; the two \
figures of merit disagree by a factor of two (",
 ButtonBox["Wiseman and Ralph, 2006",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0603062"], None}],
 "). We build both \[LongDash] an ",
 StyleBox["unsteered",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "790318be-6549-22ff-2f30-91f80cfc70c5"],
 " measurement and a ",
 StyleBox["steered",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " axis re-aimed perpendicular to the state at every step \[LongDash] and let \
the distributions settle it."
}], "Text",
 CellID->467824327,ExpressionUUID->"3e35e667-42ed-6e5d-67ca-f841769834a7"],

Cell["\<\
As loops, both share a measure-observe-update core; the steered one wraps it \
in two extra steps that recompute the axis each pass.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1012559019,ExpressionUUID->"3d92e0fe-61dd-aa06-6ba1-f9b81069f96c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Steered:", "TI"],
 " estimate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55f422cf-5719-5b56-038b-bba962ac29bc"],
 " from the past record ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Rule]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "185882f2-3bbf-8530-4867-1bbcbe4bec1a"],
 " compute ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ec07e75-02a3-3afd-36f0-703fb75788c7"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Rule]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "311eeb5e-e314-7537-6725-031b96a15c1d"],
 " choose ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "601ed991-4af3-b103-1025-d0db6e870069"],
 " perpendicular to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27a3aaa2-c993-2819-4d50-430fe8267b63"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Rule]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a4498bc-a571-157c-3a7b-11f9cc047c46"],
 " measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "\[CenterDot]", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ce0809c-d5c3-af14-749f-19d9dc77f27e"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Rule]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "319d38eb-f6c5-3702-67a2-b1b483719a68"],
 " observe ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b2144f6-69f3-9218-2adf-5db00f87e162"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Rule]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10a6d73c-c2c2-eea0-405d-cf79f774b48a"],
 " update ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["j", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3710847d-4883-61f0-5d2f-1e27693633da"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Rule]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a5dfbae-20e5-2129-7a62-f20850907073"],
 " repeat with a new ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["j", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54fe873c-afbe-d0b8-7c85-1f79ca48a282"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1427622929,ExpressionUUID->"41b5ee91-8ab8-27e2-774a-07db2f328dc8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Unsteered:", "TI"],
 " estimate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "033b6291-8419-2638-32d9-7bdb2dad8d02"],
 " from the past record ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Rule]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69bf3242-ce45-6744-1f44-b42febf04dae"],
 " measure the fixed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34f98250-b9a0-779e-5c86-241a38555de4"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Rule]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ff43cc4-be71-93f0-158b-b5ae3b05e1da"],
 " observe ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51b5abc0-0202-0151-074a-42aab7b753bb"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Rule]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "126b1bc1-46f5-8a3a-4268-92ab7281d900"],
 " update ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["j", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "046e4336-067c-8bff-2c16-5b70b30ed9c5"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Rule]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07815119-4e7f-a41e-2dbf-49436b0b0f64"],
 " repeat with the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7918a344-d32d-e3ba-2f27-3b21e6d9b180"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->115085158,ExpressionUUID->"3d8a8157-75dd-89f2-6b89-19117c69dbd8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both strategies start from the maximally mixed state and are scored by the \
same impurity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        SubscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "280c132e-a962-3439-5833-8a8bc8149f03"],
 ", which is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox["1", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c58460f-1f98-22b3-0478-58699a2d7099"],
 " when mixed and ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f9d878a-7798-33b0-35a2-1ed40212819a"],
 " when pure. Given a density matrix, define a function to compute the \
impurity:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2053577179,ExpressionUUID->"7e9a25a0-be60-edc7-26b9-bc0a3b1ab72d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"impurity", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "rho", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], 
    "/", "2"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[302]:=",
 CellID->248898466,ExpressionUUID->"3456b4ad-9984-7479-5c6d-2df718315f43"],

Cell["Set the measurement strength and the time grid:", "Text",
 CellID->538674263,ExpressionUUID->"69d1a328-4310-c880-1fee-3b7276aa9aea"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"kPur", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tickPur", " ", "=", " ", "0.01"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"span", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"tickPur", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "120"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[303]:=",
 CellID->1089240833,ExpressionUUID->"1c27efc5-dd5c-0ea0-45dc-06aed4e9548a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 StyleBox["unsteered",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " strategy measures one axis, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f9ca573-a525-e7a3-25a3-3d3cccd1cd89"],
 ", for the whole run. Each step feeds the record ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], "=", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1eda8955-2ca4-ffeb-46f9-211f4556c531"],
 " into the positivity-preserving update, and the conditioned state diffuses \
and lengthens; but as its Bloch vector swings toward the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04eee7d5-a4c3-ea8f-2c95-fe9ecd77b8d5"],
 "-axis the measurement falls into alignment and the purification slows. This \
is exactly the toolkit's ",
 Cell[BoxData["trajectory"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2fb07358-8f92-ce5d-5540-6b022a2494a7"],
 " with a fixed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "18c8dd31-1ea6-1036-48f7-d57b9b53631c"],
 " leak, so it needs no function of its own; the ensembles below call ",
 Cell[BoxData["trajectory"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "154dc22c-e6d4-21a3-4372-db8993617389"],
 " for it directly and score the result with ",
 Cell[BoxData["impurity"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00023c2b-283d-9017-3031-b67549c9e37d"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1426757747,ExpressionUUID->"495d6937-f906-8dd0-7f62-8170f8b0d73a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 StyleBox["steered",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " strategy uses the record differently. Instead of a stationary axis it \
reads the current Bloch vector off the conditioned state and measures along \
an axis ",
 StyleBox["perpendicular", "TI"],
 " to it, holding the fast ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d937789-2253-fc97-1ba1-6ed357e7c6fd"],
 " angle at every step."
}], "Text",
 CellID->892816339,ExpressionUUID->"579a3a64-9432-ab70-7db9-bc4e1dc4f65a"],

Cell["\<\
In the plainest words: look at where the qubit points now, aim the \
measurement axis perpendicular to it, make one weak measurement, update the \
state with the outcome, and repeat. The feedback is just this repeated \
re-aiming of the measurement direction, the steered chain above. The code \
never physically rotates the state with a feedback unitary (a control pulse \
applied conditioned on the record); it only changes which observable is \
measured next.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1017845166,ExpressionUUID->"194a91b0-0c16-7c4e-4f49-08faa5a34694"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One function carries the whole steered loop, with the same signature as ",
 Cell[BoxData["trajectory"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e65ff1b-2e7b-83a1-461a-f7454b0fd18b"],
 ": an initial state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2949918d-6dca-6327-5f76-08d7047f4e0d"],
 " and Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["H", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2fb7f3c1-5a6e-58a9-554c-eaab5f1b2af3"],
 ", the measurement strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "168bc571-ef41-c55f-3e88-dd3a8af5afa5"],
 ", the step ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f736822-19f9-ab87-4500-818c9f8df9ed"],
 ", the horizon ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"t", "f"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "287634d7-a493-5377-580d-ad90cd263e5d"],
 ", and a seed. Each step reads the Bloch vector, aims the axis perpendicular \
to it (the horizontal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "\[Times]", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31701ca2-f4c0-d723-670f-950ffd7aba09"],
 "), and advances the conditioned state by the positivity-preserving update. \
It returns the observer's data in ",
 Cell[BoxData["trajectory"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "42383645-cae2-5342-73c7-a82eee9721a8"],
 "'s shape, the times, states, and record, plus the axes it chose:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->649399840,ExpressionUUID->"0b11b9e5-bb8f-782a-392e-30cf3e3a4b70"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"steeredBlur", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "rho0_", ",", " ", "H_", ",", " ", "k_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "tf_",
      ",", " ", "seed_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
           RowBox[{"tf", "/", "dt"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "perp", ",", " ", 
         "dws", ",", " ", "states", ",", " ", "axes", ",", " ", "records"}], 
        "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"perp", "[", "lean_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"With", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"c", " ", "=", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Cross", "[", 
              RowBox[{"lean", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}]}], 
              "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"If", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Norm", "[", "c", "]"}], " ", "<", " ", "1.*^-6"}], ",",
              " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", "c", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
        "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{"dws", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dt", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "n"}], 
          "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{"states", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", "dw"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"With", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"leak", " ", "=", " ", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "k", "]"}], " ", 
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"perp", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "rho", "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".",
                     " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"X", ",", " ", "Y", ",", " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}], 
                   ")"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"measurementStep", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"H", ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"{", "leak", "}"}], ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[", 
                RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"measurementRecord", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"{", "leak", "}"}], ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"{", "dw", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
            "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", "rho0", ",", " ", "dws"}], "]"}]}], ";",
         "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{"axes", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"perp", "[", 
            RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
           " ", 
          RowBox[{"Most", "[", "states", "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{"records", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"measurementRecord", "[", 
             RowBox[{"#1", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "k", "]"}], " ", 
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{"#2", " ", ".", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"X", ",", " ", "Y", ",", " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}], 
                 ")"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", "#3", "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Most", "[", "states", "]"}], ",", " ", "axes", ",", " ",
              "dws"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{"<|", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"\"\<times\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
             RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<states\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "states"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<axes\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "axes"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<record\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "records"}]}], "|>"}]}]}],
       "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[304]:=",
 CellID->95053520,ExpressionUUID->"49614dfc-87d5-9726-7f1f-64a63261fa0c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In formulas: with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4eaeef1c-70dd-f5e5-7655-07460169dfcf"],
 " the current Bloch vector, each step measures the leak ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ab084b1-712e-e46c-0a4f-1dfb00d8ceb6"],
 " along a unit axis ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "009434ca-e8a5-36b3-30ab-ad9789519c99"],
 " perpendicular to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2a229ce6-e7c6-f6b5-5bd1-15c39270dc9f"],
 ". Because that axis is perpendicular to the state the signal vanishes and \
the record is pure noise,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->823893091,ExpressionUUID->"56ef6f30-06fe-ca48-7e94-877ab2889892"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], "=", "2", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "=", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["W", "TI"]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->973753736,ExpressionUUID->"3d7e8caf-dec1-3276-6b05-2508db75815c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "which is nonetheless the fast case: a state perpendicular to the axis is an \
equal superposition of the measured operator's eigenstates, where the \
back-action is strongest. The step is then the positivity-preserving \
measurement update of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2a4b2e91-3e68-2f67-5a48-c7dbbb1d724d"],
 " under ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e070ed5-18e9-e926-563c-a79f989db80c"],
 " with that record, and nothing else, with no feedback unitary; the steering \
is the re-choice of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7866ed4e-196e-bd16-281d-05289818047c"],
 " at the next node. Any direction perpendicular to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d58b19a-61e1-4a53-0b67-28c4179418b9"],
 " gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "039e17dc-7135-1c98-31a5-8e8600c066e2"],
 " and the same rate; ",
 Cell[BoxData["steeredBlur"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76f331b0-e4d2-d206-1e80-a8fd8d64a16c"],
 " takes the horizontal one, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "\[Times]", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5aa658dd-12e3-7f58-0a5e-5187a69645a2"],
 ", so the conditioned state runs in the horizontal plane while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a3641b-c972-205a-5351-7e44e80772a0"],
 " stays fixed in its tilted ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "z"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d85d5e7-830f-4689-3bba-ccc136ba2cd3"],
 "-plane, unmeasured: only the angle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06d28d0f-e448-85b2-2ee1-25688de2ef98"],
 ", never the plane the axis lies in, sets the rate. In continuous time this \
holds ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51b905fb-db49-ff7a-0746-9ca4defdc240"],
 " pathwise; at finite ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["h", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f015443-b004-ded7-453f-4e2cc1b6a43d"],
 " the residual spread is measured below. Folding from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "0"], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], "\|01d7d9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79dc6473-7f99-4552-2fe4-7e3d7a2c2fb8"],
 " over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["N", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74d8dc7d-61a6-0fac-1ce7-d627105355f6"],
 " Wiener increments, ",
 Cell[BoxData["steeredBlur"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "254b6ea2-640f-5114-5348-870c0dba207e"],
 " returns the states ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "0"], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["N", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a37b9ca-0c89-88bb-7bcc-3094a53dda81"],
 " along with the record it saw and the axes it chose."
}], "Text",
 CellID->308061613,ExpressionUUID->"57618033-75bd-c863-7d1e-1a7d7c499b49"],

Cell["\<\
Look at what the observer actually holds on one run. The record it reads is \
featureless noise, while the axes it picks swing around to stay perpendicular \
to the sharpening state:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->218833087,ExpressionUUID->"1b228fec-7489-5fb6-4ad1-26b67d3c259c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"obs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"steeredBlur", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"id2", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"0", " ", "id2"}], ",", " ", "kPur", ",", " ", "tickPur", ",", 
     " ", "1.2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
       RowBox[{"obs", "[", "\"\<record\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"DataRange", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"MinMax", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Most", "[", 
         RowBox[{"obs", "[", "\"\<times\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<record\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "Medium"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
      "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
       " ", "\"\<what the observer sees: pure noise\>\""}]}], "]"}], ",", 
    "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "@", 
       RowBox[{"obs", "[", "\"\<axes\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"DataRange", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"MinMax", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Most", "[", 
         RowBox[{"obs", "[", "\"\<times\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "Medium"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(n\), \(x\)]\)\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(n\), \(y\)]\)\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(n\), \(z\)]\)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
      "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<axis\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
      "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
       " ", "\"\<what the observer chooses: the re-aimed axis\>\""}]}], 
     "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[305]:=",
 CellID->1362785884,ExpressionUUID->"15cf7838-770d-10a7-43f5-726202b8628d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The record is a driftless noise stream: with the axis held perpendicular to \
the state, the signal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b95bd50-7b57-adaf-39aa-351a7ee3f7f5"],
 " vanishes and the meter reads pure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "216b1f6b-5cec-53ab-5768-9735549921f1"],
 ", so it shows no drift toward either eigenstate. The striking part is that \
the purification ",
 StyleBox["rate", "TI"],
 " does not depend on this record at all: the impurity falls as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", "0"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "4", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16ee990f-09f0-daa5-3e95-1169af8aa88f"],
 " on every history, the deterministic case. The geometry of the axis choices \
sets how fast the state purifies; the record's fluctuations only decide which \
of the two perpendicular eigenstates it lands on. The axis stays horizontal \
throughout (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00067b34-c3cd-1811-303e-7371f6786b7b"],
 " flat at zero) and swings in the plane to track the sharpening Bloch vector."
}], "Text",
 CellID->800074720,ExpressionUUID->"2db117d6-0b72-000c-5b4e-8e90ae075356"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The steering pins ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68a1b4b4-f7f8-1850-185e-2df1818d6aba"],
 " at every re-aiming node by construction, so the quantity worth reading is \
how far the state slips within a step before the axis resets. Pair each held \
axis with the Bloch vector at the step's ",
 StyleBox["end", "TI"],
 " and take the angle (",
 Cell[BoxData["VectorAngle"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "666da514-18bd-d59b-0e12-3d5e9949bfe1"],
 " normalizes both):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->154434508,ExpressionUUID->"29592712-3b20-e448-5f66-bf5cbedace92"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"thetaDrift", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
    RowBox[{"VectorAngle", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"obs", "[", "\"\<axes\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Rest", "[", 
        RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"obs", "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Rest", "[", 
       RowBox[{"obs", "[", "\"\<times\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      "thetaDrift"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<\[Theta] between axis and state\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Red", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"3", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameTicks", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Pi]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "None"}], "}"}], ",",
       " ", "Automatic"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<\[Theta] scatters about \[Pi]/2 within each step (the finite-h \
residue)\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[307]:=",
 CellID->1025583273,ExpressionUUID->"22115567-c1d8-2747-522f-4d40f0528dad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On average ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b71a00b-a0b6-756c-190e-3a54d1435fb6"],
 " sits on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79f35eab-5065-8c8a-2f81-57f56111d6d0"],
 ", but it scatters about it from step to step: within each interval the \
state tilts toward or away from the frozen axis before the next re-aiming \
pulls it back. That symmetric scatter, not any systematic bias, is the \
finite-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["h", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cbd088d-a6f8-eb62-1442-a1d6d372b648"],
 " residue behind the run-to-run spread measured below. The ragged opening is \
the near-mixed transient, where the Bloch vector is still near zero and \
points nowhere definite; the range clips its excursions below ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71854dcf-cc44-2a9b-27bb-64a8e5f178e1"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->194843868,ExpressionUUID->"412c5b26-c47d-b90f-70d4-5283ed090855"],

Cell["Average eighty runs of each strategy:", "Text",
 CellID->763032948,ExpressionUUID->"5f352ef2-4ae2-2c59-06ca-c7bc6e9776a3"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"unsteeredAvg", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"impurity", " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"id2", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"0", " ", "id2"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "kPur", "]"}], " ", "Z"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "tickPur", ",", " ", "1.2", ",", " ", 
          "s"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "80"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"steeredAvg", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"impurity", " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"steeredBlur", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"id2", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"0", " ", "id2"}], ",", " ", "kPur", ",", " ", "tickPur", ",",
           " ", "1.2", ",", " ", "s"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}],
       ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "80"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[309]:=",
 CellID->1903978139,ExpressionUUID->"0d7f7a51-5ff5-70fd-3b05-7c1b598042c7"],

Cell["\<\
Now visualize both purification strategies on a log scale, where a straight \
line represents exponential decay:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1178571435,ExpressionUUID->"3089d968-2504-f1ea-60b6-d1324cb6c330"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLogPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"span", ",", " ", "unsteeredAvg"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"span", ",", " ", "steeredAvg"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Joined", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<unsteered measurement\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<steered measurement\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<impurity (log scale)\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<steering purifies faster; finite steps approach the \
deterministic limit\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[311]:=",
 CellID->324779341,ExpressionUUID->"2b65a66f-d41b-de4c-591a-3848ddafa496"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The steered mean is steeper and smoother, tracking the continuous-time \
exponential more closely than the unsteered mean. But determinism is a strong \
claim: theory says the steered impurity follows ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", "0"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "4", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "428af588-0a0e-1d2d-7289-ecd2afbb6477"],
 " on ",
 StyleBox["every", "TI"],
 " record, with zero run-to-run spread, yet the simulated runs show a small \
spread and a small gap from that exponential. Is the residue real, or an \
artifact of re-aiming the axis only once per discrete step? The step is the \
suspect: within it the state drifts off ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64da9960-6030-4ffa-0cf9-114a11c515c0"],
 ", so the noise no longer cancels. If that is the cause, refining ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["h", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c687fea-7568-041a-1468-76b47c1d6f60"],
 " must shrink both the spread and the gap to the deterministic target. Test \
at the same physical time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "0.6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0cbccda1-a060-0aa2-3443-e40ad1155888"],
 " across three step sizes (each uses ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "0.6", "/", 
   StyleBox["h", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "447fe503-da77-e068-6c04-fd6cdf03b2b2"],
 " steps to reach it):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1319522016,ExpressionUUID->"708a530c-476f-43a5-208a-4b56721a118f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"finals", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Last", "[", 
             RowBox[{"impurity", " ", "/@", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"steeredBlur", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"id2", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"0", " ", "id2"}], ",", " ", "kPur", ",", " ", "h", ",",
                  " ", "0.6", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<states\>\"", 
               "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", "80", "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"target", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"0.5", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"-", "4"}], " ", "kPur", " ", "0.6"}], "]"}]}]}]}], 
        "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"h", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "finals", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "finals", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "finals", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "target"}], 
          "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"h", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.02", ",", " ", "0.01", ",", " ", "0.005"}], "}"}]}], 
      "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<step h\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<mean impurity\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<spread\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<|mean - target|\>\""}], "}"}]}],
      "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[312]:=",
 CellID->536221529,ExpressionUUID->"7c4be775-fc25-beb3-2448-ff3ef5d10499"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both the spread and the bias contract as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["h", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "144f2f1f-85ce-1d43-3c74-c7592c7b67a9"],
 " shrinks, so the residue is discretization (the finite step), not physics: \
determinism is a genuine property of the continuum limit, not something to \
read off the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], "=", "0.01"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c6a609e-b44f-cf74-146a-79d83dfb925e"],
 " grid."
}], "Text",
 CellID->327893574,ExpressionUUID->"25b14c23-2eb1-df26-534f-658d4b45a20c"],

Cell["\<\
But the mean hides the caveat, so look at the distributions. Set a four-unit \
window (400 steps) long enough that every one of the unsteered seeded runs \
reaches the target, as the explicit check below will confirm, and a count of \
200 runs:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->40368820,ExpressionUUID->"008546a0-c650-abb4-30bb-5f0df3eaf99e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"purGrid", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"tickPur", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "400"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"purN", " ", "=", " ", "200"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[313]:=",
 CellID->634400894,ExpressionUUID->"25dc0687-8bfe-aded-53e3-9fe12d88f737"],

Cell["\<\
Run the unsteered strategy over that ensemble, keeping each run's full \
impurity history:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1423111785,ExpressionUUID->"39ea782b-3727-74ef-6fea-727542d25e35"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"unsteeredRunsPur", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"impurity", " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"id2", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"0", " ", "id2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "kPur", "]"}], " ", "Z"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "tickPur", ",", " ", "4.", ",", " ", 
         "s"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "purN"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[314]:=",
 CellID->57325639,ExpressionUUID->"0337beb4-3f4a-26a7-32cc-37febafc8c8d"],

Cell["and the steered strategy the same way:", "Text",
 CellID->1374945886,ExpressionUUID->"19027a34-c886-4faa-4f32-7c71e93315f0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"steeredRunsPur", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"impurity", " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"steeredBlur", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"id2", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"0", " ", "id2"}], ",", " ", "kPur", ",", " ", "tickPur", ",",
          " ", "4.", ",", " ", "s"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "purN"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[315]:=",
 CellID->456950207,ExpressionUUID->"3a07d01d-1b7c-2a0f-6a3c-ca479e097955"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "First, compare the finite-step steered runs with the continuous-time law ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", "0"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "4", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27ef5936-9de9-9a7d-4d95-51701b9de947"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", "0"], "=", "1", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "61b66095-ece2-945e-174e-79de8494fea4"],
 ". Overlay thirty paths on the analytic exponential, on a log scale:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1460592219,ExpressionUUID->"5d61acce-ca29-858f-0b1e-45abefddefd5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLogPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Append", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"purGrid", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{"steeredRunsPur", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{";;", " ", "30"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"purGrid", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"0.5", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "4"}], " ", "kPur", " ", "purGrid"}], "]"}]}]}], 
       "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Joined", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"10", "^", 
         RowBox[{"-", "4"}]}], ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "480"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Append", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
           RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.2", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "30"}], 
       "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}]}], 
     "]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"LineLegend", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<continuous-time law\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<finite-step steered runs\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<impurity (log)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<finite-step paths fluctuate around the continuum exponential \
(dashed)\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[316]:=",
 CellID->1677337148,ExpressionUUID->"337dac42-7f47-0b68-6102-462c7af259b2"],

Cell["\<\
The paths cluster around, but do not coincide with, the dashed line at this \
step size. The refinement table above is the evidence that this cluster \
collapses onto the pathwise deterministic continuum law.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->559816626,ExpressionUUID->"3b31e76a-9cc9-3dd2-6ace-ff34157d8738"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the objective-dependence. At a ",
 StyleBox["fixed time", "TI"],
 " the steered strategy wins on the ",
 StyleBox["mean", "TI"],
 ", but the distributions show why that is subtle. Animate both ensembles as \
they purify: the steered runs stay a tight cluster sliding toward zero, while \
the unsteered runs scatter, many already purer than the steered cluster and a \
slow tail lagging behind. It is that tail, not a uniformly worse spread, that \
lifts the unsteered mean above the steered's tight, deterministic value:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->306702529,ExpressionUUID->"0462e13d-5914-5391-2c11-f96758a121fb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Animate", "[", "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Histogram", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"unsteeredRunsPur", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"steeredRunsPur", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", ".5", ",", " ", "0.01"}], "}"}], ",", 
     " ", "\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<unsteered\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<steered\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", ".5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "All"}], "}"}]}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "3"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<impurity at t = \>\"", " ", "<>", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ToString", "[", 
          RowBox[{"purGrid", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "t", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
        " ", "\"\<fraction\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
     "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<steered clusters; the unsteered runs scatter\>\""}]}], "]"}], 
   ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Length", "[", "purGrid", "]"}], "/", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AnimationRunning", " ", "->", " ", "False"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[317]:=",
 CellID->660231635,ExpressionUUID->"5fafb436-a125-8572-0554-2e73d0d1ec58"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "But the ",
 StyleBox["first-passage time", "TI"],
 " to a chosen purity tells the opposite story. For each run, record the time \
it first drops below ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptL]", "=", "0.05"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5937c2c5-33c1-e073-08cc-dbaf4675b359"],
 "; a run that does not cross within the window is left explicitly ",
 StyleBox["right-censored", "TI"],
 ", logged as still short of the target at the end rather than handed the \
endpoint as if it had crossed there:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2070365498,ExpressionUUID->"0f5c2ef4-7109-f5b8-3563-c7be00bddf82"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"fptPur", "[", "run_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"pos", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"FirstPosition", "[", 
        RowBox[{"run", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"l_", " ", "/;", " ", 
          RowBox[{"l", " ", "<", " ", "0.05"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n",
      "   ", 
     RowBox[{"If", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"MissingQ", "[", "pos", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Missing", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<RightCensored\>\"", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Length", "[", "run", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}], 
          " ", "tickPur"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"First", "[", "pos", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}], " ",
         "tickPur"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[318]:=",
 CellID->1311299970,ExpressionUUID->"249f21f6-b74e-bacc-4ca4-b8b3c2f80816"],

Cell["Collect that time for every run of each strategy:", "Text",
 CellID->1022896615,ExpressionUUID->"6d7028df-510c-978f-1b0f-c19960befdd5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"fptUnsteered", ",", " ", "fptSteer"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"fptPur", " ", "/@", " ", "unsteeredRunsPur"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"fptPur", " ", "/@", " ", "steeredRunsPur"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[319]:=",
 CellID->1963671665,ExpressionUUID->"67e8013d-d0f3-07d6-0d97-9966e0866d3c"],

Cell["\<\
Check the censor counts before computing a histogram or mean:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->949858012,ExpressionUUID->"2aeb0016-a16b-917c-5ae8-9a53d01fe046"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Count", "[", 
    RowBox[{"fptUnsteered", ",", " ", "_Missing"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Count", "[", 
    RowBox[{"fptSteer", ",", " ", "_Missing"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[320]:=",
 CellID->1295537244,ExpressionUUID->"6e2a9277-acfe-a475-1629-1430c4880f5f"],

Cell["\<\
The extended four-unit window gives zero censored runs for these seeds. If \
either count were nonzero, a plain (uncensored) average would be biased, \
ignoring the runs still short of the target, and the window would need \
extending or a survival-analysis estimate (the statistics of partly-observed \
times).\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1775107011,ExpressionUUID->"7757f304-1d73-ea00-1d6c-eb6e9407b96a"],

Cell["Histogram the two distributions:", "Text",
 CellID->1505341139,ExpressionUUID->"3fa4a1ef-0881-bd46-655b-38c9a93507ac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Histogram", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"DeleteMissing", "[", "fptUnsteered", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"DeleteMissing", "[", "fptSteer", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.2", ",", " ", "0.06"}], "}"}], ",", 
   " ", "\"\<PDF\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<unsteered\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<steered\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "3"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<first-passage time to impurity < 0.05\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<density\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<yet the unsteered measurement often reaches the target sooner\>\
\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[321]:=",
 CellID->1868278770,ExpressionUUID->"6f9797aa-fa32-a424-15ac-0ef7ffc40f0e"],

Cell["\<\
The unsteered strategy reaches down to shorter times: its runs vary, and the \
lucky ones cross the target before the steered runs. At finite step the \
steered crossing times still have a narrow distribution; under refinement \
that distribution collapses toward the continuum strategy's single \
deterministic hitting time.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->424354000,ExpressionUUID->"73356d58-d9e6-c51e-22ca-8505df90ac64"],

Cell["\<\
Compare the two means directly, fixed-time impurity against mean hitting time:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->532205865,ExpressionUUID->"7ecebc9e-fbf5-4932-26f5-35dbfd801818"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Grid", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Style", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<unsteered\>\"", ",", " ", "Bold"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Style", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<steered\>\"", ",", " ", "Bold"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Style", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<impurity at t = 0.6\>\"", ",", " ", "Bold"}], "]"}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"unsteeredRunsPur", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "61"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"steeredRunsPur", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "61"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Style", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<first-passage time to impurity < 0.05\>\"", ",", " ", 
         "Bold"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Mean", "@", 
        RowBox[{"DeleteMissing", "[", "fptUnsteered", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Mean", "@", 
        RowBox[{"DeleteMissing", "[", "fptSteer", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",",
    "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Alignment", " ", "->", " ", "Left"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Spacings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[322]:=",
 CellID->512620775,ExpressionUUID->"5942b0b3-6f6e-6b43-0f71-29fd0a1b39a9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The steered strategy has the lower fixed-time impurity but the ",
 StyleBox["longer", "TI"],
 " mean first-passage: its determinism forbids the lucky fast records that \
let an unsteered measurement occasionally reach the target early. Which \
protocol is \"optimal\" depends on the question, sharp average purity by a \
deadline or shortest typical time to a goal, and no single curve can answer \
both. This is the ",
 ButtonBox["Wiseman-Ralph",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0603062"], None}],
 " point, made by the distributions rather than asserted."
}], "Text",
 CellID->807932579,ExpressionUUID->"68dbfb54-9cec-44d9-18f8-f31e14992e23"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Feedback Cooling of a Mechanical Oscillator", "Subsection",
 CellID->243295841,ExpressionUUID->"490cd331-563c-164f-7f33-cb7b63c97c95"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The problem.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Continuously measure a mechanical oscillator's position through a cavity \
and push against its estimated motion to cool it, against a thermal bath. Its \
annihilation operator is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "657c510c-49b2-e75b-1304-49566844cda1"],
 ", and position and momentum are the dimensionless quadratures"
}], "Text",
 CellID->416937359,ExpressionUUID->"0d6ec52d-5cc9-067c-3b15-dd77557c6d46"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["b", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["b", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
     SqrtBox["2"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["b", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["b", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      SqrtBox["2"]}]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"]}], "]"}], "=", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1706026672,ExpressionUUID->"3668f576-4c14-1c4a-5e17-ed3065a16690"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "so the vacuum has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["xx",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["pp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f9031bc-85db-b36a-05af-a8e62c6f01b0"],
 " and a thermal state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["xx",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["pp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f7beb9c-7c94-54df-4518-02c675213e25"],
 ", the thermal start the covariance equations take below. The conditioned \
state obeys"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1235325005,ExpressionUUID->"61ce2c0b-0128-d3f4-17f5-c655b0c2a1de"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"d", "\[Rho]"}], "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["[",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["b", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["b", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
         StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["(",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
         StyleBox[")",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]}], ",", " ", 
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox["]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{"\|01d49f", 
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SqrtBox[
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{"\[Eta]", "k"}], "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", "2", 
       StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["W", "TI"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", "1"}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     RowBox[{"\|01d49f", 
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["b", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
     RowBox[{"\|01d49f", 
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["b", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->883233490,ExpressionUUID->"4bb1fc90-7b0c-5559-794e-f5da7eb93fa3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Watching sharpens the estimate, and the feedback force ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["f", "TI"], "\[Proportional]", "-", 
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47947242-81c8-9b15-6dac-742c3062e67f"],
 " drains the energy by opposing the motion: it takes the estimated momentum, \
which way the oscillator is heading, and pushes back, a velocity-proportional \
drag that bleeds off kinetic energy. What is left is a balance of measurement \
rate, efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e52a655-39e3-731f-4661-381fbf965e65"],
 ", gain ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["G", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e91b615-0ed0-3b31-16ae-285fab6a861b"],
 ", and heating ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "070d5859-2054-d468-2d33-520351e6beb2"],
 ". Watching alone only heats; feedback cools, but only up to an optimal gain \
beyond which it feeds the detector's noise back onto the oscillator. Cool a \
warm start, find the best gain, and sweep the detector quality."
}], "Text",
 CellID->795056725,ExpressionUUID->"2322320f-c27e-967c-52d1-b468f708fd46"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same measure-and-feedback loop cools a mechanical oscillator. The loop \
is the closed cycle of control: each step measures the oscillator's position, \
updates the running estimate of its motion, turns that estimate into a force, \
and applies it back, then repeats. Cooling takes more than watching, though: \
the loop must act. Three pieces enter now that the Kalman tracker did not \
have. A thermal bath (damping ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "043be316-2158-5fff-2dd8-fb5050ed25c5"],
 ", occupation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6802a81d-2cf4-f5d5-1831-42474486df3f"],
 ") keeps trying to warm the oscillator; the continuous position measurement \
(strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e402ad6-5057-5ed2-167f-c39061e22438"],
 ", efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41b7e238-0be5-970e-774c-0462ad91fa54"],
 ") tracks it; and a feedback force pushes back against the ",
 StyleBox["estimated", "TI"],
 " velocity, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["f", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2eb3f556-206c-8695-5640-ed10511eecff"],
 " (the conditional mean), draining energy. The state is Gaussian throughout, \
so, as in the Kalman filter, the conditional covariance is deterministic and \
the conditional mean is stochastic. This example stands alone, so fix its own \
constants:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1402288582,ExpressionUUID->"48778410-45aa-a58c-780c-1e5a6c5c0fd6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"kCool", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"etaCool", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"gammaCool", " ", "=", " ", "0.1"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"nCool", " ", "=", " ", "10."}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[323]:=",
 CellID->155652986,ExpressionUUID->"6663666a-17cc-8c5b-0e11-7834a27ed6a1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The conditional covariance is the tracking Riccati of Part Five again, now \
carrying the bath (a drift toward the thermal spread ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39cc1c7e-c0bc-15c6-6ff3-963bf1497f2c"],
 " at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d6a022c-3310-f1e4-1b69-a47646aac3ce"],
 ") and the efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a5cf6b6-efb6-dcec-7a63-eff38a40a636"],
 " on the information-gain terms, while the back-action term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c334b92-ac05-23e1-65c1-62dfc5b071cb"],
 " (the momentum kick that measuring position unavoidably costs) stays full. \
In the three entries ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
     StyleBox["xx",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
     StyleBox["xp",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
     StyleBox["pp",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "269d5917-f35c-fcc3-4ea3-515086eec629"],
 ","
}], "Text",
 CellID->1208643478,ExpressionUUID->"220c9cc5-a2c2-16ad-5233-15aed7777cf7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "(", GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
        StyleBox["xx",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]]},
      {
       SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
        StyleBox["xp",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]]},
      {
       SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
        StyleBox["pp",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]]}
     }], ")", "=", "(", GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{"2", 
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
         StyleBox["xp",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]], "-", "4", 
        StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
        SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
         StyleBox["xx",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "-", 
        StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
         StyleBox["xx",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]], "+", 
        StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", 
         FractionBox["1", "2"]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]},
      {
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
         StyleBox["pp",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]], "-", 
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
         StyleBox["xx",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]], "-", "4", 
        StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
         StyleBox["xx",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
         StyleBox["xp",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]], "-", 
        StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
         StyleBox["xp",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]]}]},
      {
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["k", "TI"], "-", "2", 
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
         StyleBox["xp",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]], "-", "4", 
        StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
        SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
         StyleBox["xp",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "-", 
        StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
         StyleBox["pp",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]], "+", 
        StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", 
         FractionBox["1", "2"]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
     }], ")"}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->346146379,ExpressionUUID->"52062e5b-b148-8aac-023d-c004c0e2d8f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "integrated from the thermal start ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["xx",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["pp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b9e800e-167b-cc53-79a5-1a68a30f96b9"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["xp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09a99be4-f821-127c-3f56-12c1f9d46146"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1804730773,ExpressionUUID->"21fc4796-9fa1-d99c-5784-5ed01a55abe6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"riccatiCool", "[", "\[Eta]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"NDSolveValue", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"vx", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"2", " ", 
          RowBox[{"vc", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "kCool", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"vx", "[", "t", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"gammaCool", " ", 
          RowBox[{"vx", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"gammaCool", " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"nCool", " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"vc", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"vp", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"vx", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "kCool", " ", 
          RowBox[{"vx", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"vc", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"gammaCool", " ", 
          RowBox[{"vc", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"vp", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"vc", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", "kCool", " ", "-", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "kCool", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"vc", "[", "t", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"gammaCool", " ", 
          RowBox[{"vp", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"gammaCool", " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"nCool", " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"vx", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{"nCool", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"vc", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0."}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"vp", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{"nCool", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"vx", ",", " ", "vc", ",", " ", "vp"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "80"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[324]:=",
 CellID->102052525,ExpressionUUID->"3ea97580-6bed-1077-6657-6cea0d98635d"],

Cell["\<\
The steady covariance, read off the late-time solution, is the sharpest the \
observer can ever know the oscillator:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1286127511,ExpressionUUID->"345a0710-bfec-3876-5c79-9f5a399e8b5c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"steadyCovCool", "[", "\[Eta]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Through", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"riccatiCool", "[", "\[Eta]", "]"}], "[", "80.", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[325]:=",
 CellID->1085349338,ExpressionUUID->"56a4078a-bfa3-4726-7e5b-9ed43a562a0c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Take its three entries at perfect efficiency, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26fb0827-d9bf-287b-4e98-a180d84a7b41"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->884952081,ExpressionUUID->"5706a8dc-de84-4347-7d3d-4199db3111ad"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"vxCool", ",", " ", "vcCool", ",", " ", "vpCool"}], "}"}], " ", "=",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"steadyCovCool", "[", "etaCool", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[326]:=",
 CellID->592254278,ExpressionUUID->"2d69e98f-64de-6fdb-5b16-00e90d6b3521"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its mean phonon number (the count of vibrational quanta) is the ",
 StyleBox["conditional floor", "TI"],
 ", the lowest occupation the record can pin down:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1827832951,ExpressionUUID->"168d2c40-6f69-6af1-3eb2-c62a0a1c38db"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"condFloorCool", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"vxCool", " ", "+", " ", "vpCool"}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-",
     " ", "0.5"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[327]:=",
 CellID->1018133995,ExpressionUUID->"5ba2698e-fe1d-1d69-0951-80ebfba867b3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Kalman gains ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["xx",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ea67a49-9063-84e3-365e-7c132117eec9"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["xp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58f54a37-a74b-68c6-088b-6c70d2fe3a2c"],
 " set how hard each record increment steers the estimate:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2045666246,ExpressionUUID->"75e1b769-bd43-d492-239e-2f3334f7bef8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"kxCool", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "kCool", "]"}], " ", "vxCool"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"kpCool", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "kCool", "]"}], " ", "vcCool"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[328]:=",
 CellID->1382967107,ExpressionUUID->"6ca9690d-8fe0-3108-1456-8157299a8052"],

Cell["\<\
Here is the key point, and the reason watching alone is not cooling: averaged \
over all records, the unconditional occupation is the conditional floor plus \
the spread of the estimate about it.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1417511298,ExpressionUUID->"647c50fc-34e3-bac8-0c04-49a6bc970812"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The conditional mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26f185d1-6f58-e3b1-4e8e-1c9b0ad2b19b"],
 " follows a linear stochastic differential equation (SDE) driven by the \
innovation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2068c8a6-f8a3-ae64-5017-e103f957f54e"],
 " (the unpredicted part of the record),"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1457683890,ExpressionUUID->"71e08206-fd12-5e06-279f-2463f4a7256c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "=", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["G", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["K", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["W", "TI"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["G", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{"-", 
         StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
        StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]},
       {
        RowBox[{"-", 
         StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}], 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "2", "-", 
         StyleBox["G", "TI"]}]}
      }], ")"}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["K", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
       {
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["x", "TI"]]},
       {
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["p", "TI"]]}
      }], ")"}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->858004867,ExpressionUUID->"0d887537-d4d2-c16f-3b88-6d70dd6493b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "component by component (with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f5790be-8388-a9de-756c-09f83622fb24"],
 " here),"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1157433805,ExpressionUUID->"3df4e37b-637b-fece-6b8b-fb25160fc414"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox[
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], 
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["W", "TI"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"-", 
        StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
        StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         FractionBox[
          StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
         StyleBox["G", "TI"]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
        StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["W", "TI"], "."}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->796928914,ExpressionUUID->"4a3f75be-20c7-75c2-7bc5-6cf851725f28"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The drift ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["G", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3be838d6-abbf-bcfe-6997-b193ce4b06c4"],
 " is the closed loop written out: the off-diagonal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4edd261b-067a-5094-76e2-b845b30f22fe"],
 " is the free rotation, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "037c0c65-d4c7-b425-3103-a64edd731f0f"],
 " on the diagonal is bath damping, and the lone ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["G", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "574a8c08-e927-fc17-7d49-265588d3c77d"],
 " on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "661d9b09-967b-e29f-0e22-1353230fb0e5"],
 " row is the feedback; the gains ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["p", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"2", 
     SqrtBox[
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
      StyleBox["xx",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     SqrtBox[
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
      StyleBox["xp",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50592a6e-077b-04ad-0066-cc48b20e6ef7"],
 " are the ones just defined. Averaged over records, the covariance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ae9de12-c3c6-bf78-7a96-d05ff6700242"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c131b6b-6556-d251-4420-93350ce0a0bb"],
 " obeys"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1009699246,ExpressionUUID->"663ec209-2bde-9ee1-0fc5-e4534e68e4cb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], "."], "=", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["G", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["K", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["K", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1843094008,ExpressionUUID->"4646ec1c-7bb4-e85c-6e7d-06467e46baa6"],

Cell["and at steady state,", "Text",
 CellID->2053559494,ExpressionUUID->"009fa45f-c653-9503-30a4-3e18f3e7fc69"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["G", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["K", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["K", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "=", "0"}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1533578161,ExpressionUUID->"0df8e50a-e098-808a-3b87-fd579112d2d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "the continuous Lyapunov equation, with the rank-one Kalman-gain noise ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["K", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "=", "(", GridBox[{
     {
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["p", "TI"]]}]},
     {
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["p", "TI"]]}], 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"]}
    }], ")"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e2e8d5f-1666-371d-07d5-2519a3109a67"],
 ", solved by:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->876660136,ExpressionUUID->"156af067-c7e0-b0e6-4369-ea40f19a02cc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"nUncCool", "[", "gg_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"LyapunovSolve", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "gammaCool"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], 
           ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "gammaCool"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
              "gg"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"-", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"kxCool", "^", "2"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"kxCool", " ", "kpCool"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"kxCool", " ", "kpCool"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"kpCool", "^", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"s", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         "vxCool", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"s", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         "vpCool"}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "0.5"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[329]:=",
 CellID->1974583224,ExpressionUUID->"4bf44795-0096-4fae-798c-5edfb12315f4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With no feedback, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6df0ebcc-3ebb-64ea-1b8f-0296bb4e4e30"],
 ", watching does not cool at all: it ",
 StyleBox["heats", "TI"],
 ", because measurement back-action kicks the momentum and nothing removes \
the energy. Confirm this two ways, the conditional-plus-spread bookkeeping \
against the plain unconditional master equation (back-action on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
   StyleBox["pp",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b24542a-2937-2c7d-6adc-4e7448c27747"],
 ", bath, no information gain):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->761010835,ExpressionUUID->"2b2c6ce5-e2d3-dbc3-5ad3-85ce9767a929"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"nUncCool", "[", "0.", "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"u", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"NDSolveValue", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"vx", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"2", " ", 
              RowBox[{"vc", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
             RowBox[{"gammaCool", " ", 
              RowBox[{"vx", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"gammaCool", " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"nCool", " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"vc", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"vp", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
             RowBox[{"vx", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
             RowBox[{"gammaCool", " ", 
              RowBox[{"vc", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"vp", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", 
              RowBox[{"vc", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", "kCool", " ", "-",
              " ", 
             RowBox[{"gammaCool", " ", 
              RowBox[{"vp", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"gammaCool", " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"nCool", " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"vx", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
            RowBox[{"nCool", " ", "+", " ", "0.5"}]}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"vc", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0."}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"vp", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
            RowBox[{"nCool", " ", "+", " ", "0.5"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"vx", ",", " ", "vp"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "200"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"u", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "[", "200.", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"u", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "[", "200.", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
       "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "0.5"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[330]:=",
 CellID->1273215491,ExpressionUUID->"47b8b786-9b5d-56d3-6d47-2ee01ee83c39"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both give the same number, above the bath's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "=", "10"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39ca63f1-5b29-ac93-6fca-7abb5eddf6f9"],
 ": the meter alone leaves the oscillator hotter than it found it."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1918360181,ExpressionUUID->"4ddb3fe8-f924-fde1-7bf8-b6b5f8d6c7cb"],

Cell["\<\
Now close the loop. The conditional mean is a stochastic trajectory driven by \
the innovation, with the feedback force damping the momentum estimate:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->905478106,ExpressionUUID->"1a3c3edd-6533-5c23-4bc3-b7870cc62709"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Gcool", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"dtCool", " ", "=", " ", "0.01"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"nStepCool", " ", "=", " ", "2500"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"timesCool", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"dtCool", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nStepCool"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[331]:=",
 CellID->1698065530,ExpressionUUID->"6e06e0ed-b7e1-fe10-163d-f9b6c195c57a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "092132f0-8112-8068-38de-abba30a4d2b2"],
 " the oscillator is thermal, so the total covariance is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", "1", "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\|01d7d9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47a7abaa-7c0e-d713-6d5c-42f475b8ba79"],
 ". That total splits into the conditional floor the filter always carries \
plus the spread of the estimate about it, so the means must be drawn with the \
full ",
 StyleBox["difference", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\|01d7d9", "-", "\[CapitalSigma]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6059b901-cdf2-bf42-1066-316aeb8405a8"],
 ", including its off-diagonal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["xp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64b436e8-4ec1-9688-0c4b-afb26b75fcd2"],
 ", to avoid double-counting the initial uncertainty and to make the initial \
unconditional state exactly thermal (the conditional covariance ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalSigma]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e284bac-efa5-b7a3-6628-62098a511d89"],
 " is held at its steady value throughout, the filter assumed already settled \
at its steady covariance, so the cooling transient sits entirely in the \
mean-spread ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "223ac921-909b-296a-53d9-e08b212e7bb0"],
 "):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->149360148,ExpressionUUID->"64f5a232-c990-b984-0c8a-447fe82a0bee"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"meanRunCool", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gg_", ",", " ", "seed_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"init", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
           RowBox[{"MultinormalDistribution", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{
                 "nCool", " ", "+", " ", "0.5", " ", "-", " ", "vxCool"}], ",",
                  " ", 
                 RowBox[{"-", "vcCool"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"-", "vcCool"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{
                 "nCool", " ", "+", " ", "0.5", " ", "-", " ", "vpCool"}]}], 
                "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"kicks", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
             RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dtCool", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            "nStepCool"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"xp", ",", " ", "dw"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"xp", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"xp", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"gammaCool", "/", "2"}], " ", 
                  RowBox[{"xp", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", "dtCool"}],
               " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{"kxCool", " ", "dw"}]}], ",", "\n", "       ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"xp", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"-", 
                  RowBox[{"xp", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"gammaCool", "/", "2"}], " ", 
                  RowBox[{"xp", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"gg", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"xp", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", "dtCool"}],
               " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{"kpCool", " ", "dw"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
         "     ", "init", ",", " ", "kicks"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[332]:=",
 CellID->990508151,ExpressionUUID->"4b797f7f-c7ba-1604-7907-7738f24f7d6e"],

Cell["\<\
The unconditional occupation in time is the ensemble spread of these means \
plus the conditional floor. Average over an ensemble of runs:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->472375463,ExpressionUUID->"45ea52ef-3554-0907-73ea-4bc9bce1586d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nEnsCool", " ", "=", " ", "120"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[333]:=",
 CellID->1352706751,ExpressionUUID->"5aa94cfa-2f23-80a7-0a57-65a44ad7d28d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a feedback gain, ",
 Cell[BoxData["nDrainCool"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "080683ca-9499-65d9-383d-1a941d2c4f23"],
 " runs that ensemble and returns the occupation at each sampled time, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["xx",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "+", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
     StyleBox["xx",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["pp",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "+", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
     StyleBox["pp",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["]",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], "-", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f690331-eebc-872f-3516-9b7a8b4eea75"],
 ", the mean-spread ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65e95d55-a99f-bfd5-1397-551ec82b053f"],
 " (read off as the ensemble variance of each conditional mean) added to the \
conditional floor ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalSigma]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e95e83b-0d9e-83fb-06aa-0265a428d1c1"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->890986319,ExpressionUUID->"5f578f4c-339a-d4b8-056c-2716462cbe82"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"nDrainCool", "[", "gg_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"ens", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"meanRunCool", "[", 
          RowBox[{"gg", ",", " ", "s"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "nEnsCool"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Variance", "[", 
            RowBox[{"ens", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "j", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
            "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "vxCool", " ", "+", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Variance", "[", 
            RowBox[{"ens", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "j", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
            "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "vpCool"}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-", 
        " ", "0.5"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"nStepCool", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "25"}], "}"}]}],
       "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[334]:=",
 CellID->1572592159,ExpressionUUID->"1d7a39f5-2f84-924e-4b19-b0bf4a36e094"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Track it with the loop open (gain ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "59677bcb-6d95-6f1d-0f1d-729504203267"],
 ") and closed (gain ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["G", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56ec6282-f98a-b15f-7e94-7beff83c03a5"],
 "):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->523613550,ExpressionUUID->"40fbad85-d3f9-d70d-7098-44eee58dba57"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"coolOff", ",", " ", "coolOn"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"nDrainCool", "[", "0.", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nDrainCool", "[", "Gcool", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[335]:=",
 CellID->506908930,ExpressionUUID->"47eae38a-28ac-69e2-6de9-fad449593bc8"],

Cell["\<\
Now visualize the cooling: the occupation with the loop off (heating above \
the bath) and on (draining toward, but not reaching, the conditional floor):\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->783859841,ExpressionUUID->"3d21e4c2-12f3-8786-64de-fdaca687edec"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"timesCool", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", ";;", " ", "25"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
        " ", "coolOff"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"timesCool", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", ";;", " ", "25"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
        " ", "coolOn"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<loop open (watching only)\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<loop closed (feedback)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<phonon number\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<feedback cools; watching alone heats\>\""}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", "97", "]"}], "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        "Dashed"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nCool"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Last", "@", "timesCool"}], ",", " ", "nCool"}], "}"}]}], 
        "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", "97", "]"}], "[", "4", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        "Dashed"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "condFloorCool"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Last", "@", "timesCool"}], ",", " ", "condFloorCool"}], 
          "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[336]:=",
 CellID->836234808,ExpressionUUID->"72da8a28-c018-2074-22f9-2c75f1ad735e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The mean phonon number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["b", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57df3a4c-b574-c457-7de4-bc163c06aebd"],
 " is the oscillator's stored energy in quanta of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56b731d2-b1dc-5164-7e4c-a89fc069204e"],
 ", so a higher curve is a hotter oscillator and a lower one colder; cooling \
drives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0758e084-cdd2-0fbb-2d67-f9e1e4675581"],
 " down toward the ground state. The open loop climbs above the thermal line \
(green); the closed loop drains fast and settles well below it, above the \
conditional floor (red)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->410625993,ExpressionUUID->"53f282fc-d9f3-c4a2-0181-1bb9df87ae88"],

Cell["\<\
The occupation plot shows that the loop cools, but not how. Take it apart, \
from a single record to the whole ensemble.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->230379626,ExpressionUUID->"065deb70-832e-a04f-2e62-033a36d8f295"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Start with one record seen twice. The quantity that separates watching from \
cooling is the energy carried by the center of the estimate, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["center",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023a3ab5-9b7c-3e4c-33d9-b3ff1e0e8496"],
 ", formed step by step from a run:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->26532680,ExpressionUUID->"0950ae2c-fd95-e5a5-3f6f-4789f421cf8f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"centerEnergy", "[", "run_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"#", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"#", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], 
      " ", "&"}], ")"}], " ", "/@", " ", "run"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[337]:=",
 CellID->1009717036,ExpressionUUID->"63d73e3d-5e6d-9b2c-11ec-b0675b19e676"],

Cell["\<\
A fixed seed draws the same starting point and the same noise kicks at any \
gain, so running one seed with the loop open and then closed holds the \
disturbance fixed and leaves the feedback as the only difference between the \
two histories:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->151019001,ExpressionUUID->"19261c33-408d-2b93-48dd-967d713879f9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"recOff", ",", " ", "recOn"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"meanRunCool", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"meanRunCool", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Gcool", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[338]:=",
 CellID->1656643860,ExpressionUUID->"61f29a52-27f6-2d9f-1781-1c1c518377e5"],

Cell["\<\
Lay the two center energies on one axis, the open record against the closed \
one:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->24370237,ExpressionUUID->"39b8808a-080a-fb1f-6f47-19d4a9bcc665"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"timesCool", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"centerEnergy", "[", "recOff", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"timesCool", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"centerEnergy", "[", "recOn", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
   ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<loop open (same noise)\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<loop closed (same noise)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<center energy\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<same record: feedback drains the estimate's energy\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[339]:=",
 CellID->730383262,ExpressionUUID->"01c3b6b5-4696-f194-37f0-2fff7320c3fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both traces start together. The open one wanders and stays high, since the \
bath damps the mean only at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41915581-04ed-47bc-77af-4cebac982d86"],
 ", far too slowly to remove the energy the noise pours in; the closed one, \
under the identical noise, is pulled down within a couple of periods and \
holds low. Same disturbance, opposite fate: the loop turns the record into a \
force that carries energy out."
}], "Text",
 CellID->304869518,ExpressionUUID->"3329119b-60db-b2d6-62d6-88c5116f003c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How much energy? The feedback force ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1615cf65-d1a2-5497-3e2a-e74ee0573efd"],
 " opposes the velocity, so it does work at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cd77268-421f-8518-44ed-743277abec62"],
 ". Accumulate that rate along the closed record for the energy removed by \
time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47ae9621-0454-0efb-6d55-0f8bade154c1"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["removed",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "750c318a-354e-3de3-2333-a8d4bcf887c9"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1481638679,ExpressionUUID->"31301a4b-de00-df4c-60cf-9c14dbbaa596"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"extractedWork", "[", 
    RowBox[{"run_", ",", " ", "gg_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gg", " ", "dtCool", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Accumulate", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"#", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "&"}], ")"}], 
        " ", "/@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Most", "[", "run", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "0."}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[340]:=",
 CellID->1624629187,ExpressionUUID->"7bf891b7-a846-9636-2987-08f0c9f0fd1c"],

Cell["Plot that running total along the closed record:", "Text",
 CellID->251976942,ExpressionUUID->"470c2033-8417-1ad4-6d33-ba7d2da2683e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"timesCool", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"extractedWork", "[", 
       RowBox[{"recOn", ",", " ", "Gcool"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<energy removed by feedback\>\""}],
      "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<cooling is a steady drain, not a one-time act\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[341]:=",
 CellID->1001631779,ExpressionUUID->"5ad9af22-3fdb-49f9-0ae6-468cba6e1bc3"],

Cell["\<\
The curve climbs and never flattens, and the work it reports far outruns the \
few units the estimate's energy actually fell. That gap is the mechanism: \
measurement back-action and the bath keep pouring energy in, and the feedback \
keeps taking it back out. Once the oscillator is cold the loop does not stop; \
it runs on to hold it there, the shock absorber built from a measurement, \
doing work forever against the noise.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->131866538,ExpressionUUID->"4cf910a9-0c85-fbc1-7486-89f3a531c92b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One record is one draw; cooling is a statement about the whole ensemble. \
From each of many records at a fixed gain, take the endpoint of the \
estimate's center, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "452c77a0-bd62-5a53-6cd4-6e0a341728b9"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2120574329,ExpressionUUID->"433c54f0-eae1-518a-72c4-4dbd8e9423d0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"cloudCool", "[", "gg_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"meanRunCool", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gg", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ")"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", "nEnsCool", "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[342]:=",
 CellID->905900721,ExpressionUUID->"60391242-a9f1-d17d-11c6-942fcf85a047"],

Cell["\<\
Scatter that cloud of endpoints, the loop open against closed:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->30454613,ExpressionUUID->"41c69146-bf62-c611-77fd-09203a14ad7b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"cloudCool", "[", "0.", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"cloudCool", "[", "Gcool", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.5", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<loop open\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<loop closed\>\""}], "}"}]}], 
   ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<<x>\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<<p>\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<feedback pulls the cloud of estimates in\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[343]:=",
 CellID->936073442,ExpressionUUID->"5c6c9045-c767-8f66-0413-0a2ef213d24c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The open-loop centers sprawl across phase space, still spreading because \
nothing damps them; the closed-loop centers collapse into a tight knot at the \
origin. That knot is the mean-spread ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54c0d9f6-8cd5-48f4-7cff-d0b025601ade"],
 ", the covariance of where the estimate sits across records, and feedback is \
what pulls it in."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2004769691,ExpressionUUID->"10c2afdf-1c4a-6aca-40f1-469995ff3810"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The knot is only part of the uncertainty. What an outside observer sees is \
that spread ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e6400ee-92df-7263-561b-99c8276a4149"],
 " blurred by the conditional floor ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalSigma]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a2c3e4c-43bd-aee6-1bd3-b0167649f4cc"],
 ", how sharply the filter knows each single history, the two adding to the \
total covariance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]", "+", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2da42c23-5972-22c8-5b5b-c58d58077012"],
 ". Assemble the conditional floor ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalSigma]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c8af9dd-094d-d766-4489-f087a8f9ba4c"],
 " from the three steady entries found above:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1569231351,ExpressionUUID->"7cc0f9d1-2fd7-9dda-24ff-f09b4a63e720"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"condCovCool", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"vxCool", ",", " ", "vcCool"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"vcCool", ",", " ", "vpCool"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[344]:=",
 CellID->1612045584,ExpressionUUID->"6090c20f-1226-92f3-10af-e469a7d0e0d9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The mean-spread ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05991ec7-58a0-3f5d-33a6-97a1595a85a7"],
 " solves the Lyapunov balance of the previous block, so it is exact, with no \
sampling:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1224848414,ExpressionUUID->"0d6d1e2a-2e52-ea78-3b12-90744be4b942"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"spreadCool", "[", "gg_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"LyapunovSolve", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "gammaCool"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "\n", "     ", 
         "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "gammaCool"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "gg"}]}], 
        "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"kxCool", "^", "2"}], ",", " ", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"kxCool", " ", "kpCool"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"kxCool", " ", "kpCool"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"kpCool", "^", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[345]:=",
 CellID->152101747,ExpressionUUID->"514c4c6c-8022-d8b7-0774-663631d4aa9d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Draw the one-sigma ellipse of the floor ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalSigma]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68df41a8-6354-4794-18e5-58f216e12dfe"],
 " alone and of the total ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]", "+", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6341ee00-46aa-0ad7-117e-006a735f583d"],
 " with the loop open and closed:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1101372283,ExpressionUUID->"51765390-551f-8be6-070e-4ada5cabd9cc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"covarianceEllipse", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"condCovCool", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"spreadCool", "[", "0.", "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"covarianceEllipse", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"condCovCool", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"spreadCool", "[", "Gcool", "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"covarianceEllipse", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "condCovCool"}], 
      "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<<x>\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<<p>\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<feedback shrinks the total toward the fixed floor\>\""}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<total \[CapitalSigma]+S, open-loop\>\"", ",", " ", "\n", 
      "   ", "\"\<total \[CapitalSigma]+S, closed-loop\>\"", ",", " ", "\n", 
      "   ", "\"\<conditional floor \[CapitalSigma]\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[346]:=",
 CellID->137398679,ExpressionUUID->"651ec994-b5cc-7852-1325-e0de3c794ab8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two total ellipses are the whole state the world sees; the third is the \
conditional floor ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalSigma]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04ab5aad-5ed8-49aa-2ca9-53f75b6d1bf0"],
 " by itself, the uncertainty the filter keeps on every single history. \
Closing the loop shrinks the total from the wide open-loop ellipse to the \
much smaller closed-loop one, but even that halts at the floor and cannot \
cross it. The floor itself is identical open and closed: feedback is a \
Hamiltonian, so it moves where the estimate sits, never how sharply the \
filter knows it, shrinking ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f9eb20d-625d-c280-65a5-345717e990ea"],
 " alone and leaving ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalSigma]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62e46a02-3a5b-686c-129b-8c6cbfee3ab6"],
 " fixed. The gap between the closed-loop ellipse and the floor is the \
residual the next plot minimizes over the gain; that floor is the cold that \
no gain can beat."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1953556957,ExpressionUUID->"5622c27e-fa64-d20c-7fd1-e43bff16a156"],

Cell["\<\
How hard should the loop push? Sweep the gain and read the steady occupation \
off the exact Lyapunov balance:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->943903693,ExpressionUUID->"71a9abed-5fb9-62e0-2756-42b75a4c30ca"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gainsCool", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "12", ",", " ", "0.1"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"gainsCool", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"nUncCool", " ", "/@", " ", "gainsCool"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<feedback gain G\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<steady phonon number\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<an optimal gain: too little leaves it warm, too much feeds \
noise back\>\""}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", "97", "]"}], "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        "Dashed"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nCool"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Last", "@", "gainsCool"}], ",", " ", "nCool"}], "}"}]}], 
        "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", "97", "]"}], "[", "4", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        "Dashed"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "condFloorCool"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Last", "@", "gainsCool"}], ",", " ", "condFloorCool"}], 
          "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[347]:=",
 CellID->292818558,ExpressionUUID->"61558bcf-8725-3a67-176a-22a932d1894d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The occupation falls steeply from the heated open-loop value, reaches a \
minimum near the gain chosen above, then rises again. Beyond the optimum the \
loop feeds the estimate's own measurement noise back onto the oscillator: \
this is the imprecision-back-action tradeoff, between the shot-noise blur on \
the record (the ",
 StyleBox["imprecision", "TI"],
 ") and the momentum kick that reading the position costs (the back-action), \
and it caps every real feedback-cooling experiment. It never reaches the \
conditional floor (red): that would need a noiseless actuator, the element \
that applies the feedback force, acting on a perfectly known state."
}], "Text",
 CellID->264739147,ExpressionUUID->"5da858a5-47c1-808d-0ba8-510f7275d2d7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Finally, a better detector lowers both the floor and the achievable cold. \
Repeat the floor-plus-spread Lyapunov balance at efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f9bb61a-aee2-f350-65b8-2847ca94c1ba"],
 ", where the conditional covariance sharpens and the gain becomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"\[Eta]", "k"}], "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CapitalSigma]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4e748159-8484-6d12-760b-19032d313478"],
 ", holding ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["G", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7930e290-b167-c2f9-28cf-fbddc01390c3"],
 " fixed at its ideal-detector value (not re-optimized per ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fb17bb4-4674-882a-654f-72fe7306db70"],
 ", so the cooled curve is conservative at low ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "28bf2227-b714-1237-5844-bb80c2a1611d"],
 "):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1237098126,ExpressionUUID->"3b8c3639-ce66-7d16-69b3-a862eb13447c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"nUncCoolEta", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Eta]_", ",", " ", "gg_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"c", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"steadyCovCool", "[", "\[Eta]", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "kx", ",", 
       " ", "kp", ",", " ", "s"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"kx", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", "kCool"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"c", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"kp", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", "kCool"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"c", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"LyapunovSolve", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "gammaCool"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], 
           ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "gammaCool"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
              "gg"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"kx", "^", "2"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"kx", " ", "kp"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"kx", " ", "kp"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"kp", "^", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
      "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"s", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"c", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"s", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"c", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ",
        "0.5"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[349]:=",
 CellID->294194286,ExpressionUUID->"3a55be4f-f4c1-c728-6a6a-3028fd75aa72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Sweep the efficiency from a poor detector, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "0.2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "408944f1-25be-34c3-70b7-5dbb4c489e29"],
 ", to a perfect one:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->757102330,ExpressionUUID->"6769d722-bdd2-9791-0d16-ce8c3464fdfb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"etasCool", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0.2", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0.01"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[350]:=",
 CellID->296089063,ExpressionUUID->"0930076b-5510-ea29-38cf-9f355caab973"],

Cell["\<\
Plot the conditional floor and the fixed-gain cooled occupation against \
efficiency:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1606580443,ExpressionUUID->"66fe4c41-b67c-2d6f-0e86-662ac30977b5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"etasCool", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"#", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{"#", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-", 
           " ", "0.5"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"steadyCovCool", " ", "/@", " ", "etasCool"}], ")"}]}]}], 
       "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"etasCool", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"nUncCoolEta", "[", 
           RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "Gcool"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
         " ", "etasCool"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<conditional floor\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<cooled occupation (fixed gain)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<detector efficiency\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<phonon number\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<a better detector cools colder\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[351]:=",
 CellID->2086732509,ExpressionUUID->"08adeec7-f156-e6d0-3852-07a080e0cc3a"],

Cell["\<\
Both curves fall as the detector improves, and the gap between them is the \
price of noisy actuation. This is measurement-based cooling of a \
nanomechanical drum or a levitated nanoparticle toward its ground state, not \
by contact with something colder but by watching precisely and pushing back: \
the same conditional covariance that told the Kalman filter how well it could \
track now sets how cold the feedback can pull.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1259953946,ExpressionUUID->"64d088ea-03f9-e45d-0cef-21b4b58dcea7"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Part Seven: Two Bookkeepings, and the Colour of the Light", "Section",
 CellID->544170496,ExpressionUUID->"6f15138c-0e8c-8125-152a-8ad6ab3ed00f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Linear vs Nonlinear: One Trajectory, Two Descriptions", "Subsection",
 CellID->186431800,ExpressionUUID->"405f258f-ff79-d7cb-7064-bce8fa0dbd11"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The problem.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " One diffusive history, written under two probability measures. Under a \
reference Wiener measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03e55ba9-fe94-2332-319b-52f2fb268e18"],
 ", the ",
 StyleBox["linear", "TI"],
 " stochastic Schrodinger equation runs an unnormalized state under plain \
noise,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->480122852,ExpressionUUID->"2a76882c-12fa-ddf2-5a0d-2276a68ca7d8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], "=", 
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"]}], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["1", "2"], 
      RowBox[{
       UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"],
        LimitsPositioning->False], 
       RowBox[{
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "."}]}]}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1734463933,ExpressionUUID->"4d3ef6c8-e314-d687-74c5-ef9596a6bced"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its squared norm is the Radon-Nikodym likelihood density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["Q", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "743a182c-0f06-6831-1dd9-9276aab33b1b"],
 " of the physical record measure relative to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "42c100d4-e672-0739-72fe-999193076a03"],
 " up to that time, not an absolute probability for one continuous record. \
Under the physical measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["P", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06047db6-ee6f-8c38-2e3c-74f38b1bd702"],
 ", the normalized master equation is driven by the innovation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11613fd8-84a9-9cd5-471e-b6822d5de63f"],
 " of the observed increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "42148f44-8d63-ba11-722b-272e2417097b"],
 ","
}], "Text",
 CellID->1234622209,ExpressionUUID->"15b08668-721a-3691-434f-183207ac9cfb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["W", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{"2", "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["Re",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["Tr",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["[",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox["]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->231537097,ExpressionUUID->"29a1e51d-1380-e9cf-5f5e-fd47a63abb15"],

Cell["\<\
The useful fact is that the reference-measure average of the unnormalized \
projectors is the master-equation state. Build the linear version and check.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->98463751,ExpressionUUID->"21898f1f-7ce2-17d9-57b6-275974977d23"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One diffusive trajectory has two equivalent descriptions. The ",
 StyleBox["nonlinear",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " SME (used so far) carries the normalized state and renormalizes each step. \
The ",
 StyleBox["linear",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " SSE carries an unnormalized state under the zero-drift reference noise ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4692cd91-7435-14b3-6ea1-e4db7dc07e99"],
 ", the noise of a reference measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "000a09f6-5b3f-ef45-3009-a0b05ecbb5af"],
 " that reads every record as signal-free noise, and never renormalizes,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->753959217,ExpressionUUID->"29133634-70e6-2af3-5f20-a87e009378d9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     TemplateBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
      "Ket"]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"-", 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
        FractionBox["1", "2"], 
        SuperscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      TemplateBox[{
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
       "Ket"], 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
      TemplateBox[{
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
       "Ket"], 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["J", "TI"]}]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"d", "J"}], "TI"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]], " ", 
     StyleBox["under",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["Q", "TI"], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->294573205,ExpressionUUID->"59a11c54-6c5b-70c2-0f5e-961e05ee4228"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two facts turn this single equation into the section. Its squared norm ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["w", "TI"], "=", 
   TemplateBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
    "BraKet"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2480a9a0-11fa-1869-4cbf-400aa78f6ab3"],
 " is the likelihood ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["Q", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4bc2c5e6-2df7-f0b4-79f1-dcc04b83c29e"],
 " that reweights ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d4459f2-9267-9bdb-5b7c-50bc2713e921"],
 " into the physical measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["P", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2830cc4d-ff27-6d9e-59cf-e616fad237e4"],
 "; and the plain ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "28a95ddb-d98e-e41c-5857-5484d838cf66"],
 "-average of the unnormalized projectors ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
    "Bra"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0df78371-259d-4014-3b8c-1b3b4c28137e"],
 " is the master-equation state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2757147d-ed01-5031-4d6c-8e2684b4231b"],
 ", carried with no reweighting. Take the average first, the weight second."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1849429623,ExpressionUUID->"0d7703a7-7e82-d2bb-3b0c-9a017b34a081"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The average is two lines of Ito calculus. With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "313bd3d6-a81b-5e6e-60d8-ca93c9ae24b4"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], "2"], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25416759-7698-4697-537f-7f03032d2cfd"],
 ", the drift terms collect into the Lindbladian and the noise into one \
trace-free term,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2063060035,ExpressionUUID->"0a04e1f2-9872-3cce-3a3b-f8bc19048614"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], "=", "\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], "+", 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1518183935,ExpressionUUID->"55e5145d-e893-2f9b-039a-8e06892675e1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Under ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ed6f41e-2589-ab78-16ed-ee584c3df642"],
 " the increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3da09602-cd29-7167-6b5f-086fe4dc404d"],
 " has zero mean, so averaging erases the stochastic term and the mean \
unnormalized state obeys the master equation on its own, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox["\|01d53c", 
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "\[ScriptCapitalL]", "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox["\|01d53c", 
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "513edd1a-c798-2d92-00c5-d547f22d77f8"],
 ", hence ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\|01d53c", 
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "785f55ac-af04-4296-2865-4c09cab110fc"],
 ". Fix the atom and the non-Hermitian drift ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "052128e6-0c43-261a-2cde-c1c0a5f78d60"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->18082725,ExpressionUUID->"7e2f36be-77c2-3eec-27d4-aff802748436"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]lin", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"cLin", " ", "=", " ", "lower"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Knh", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]lin", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], " ", "-", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "cLin", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
      "cLin"}], "/", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"step", " ", "=", " ", "0.005"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"steps", " ", "=", " ", "600"}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[352]:=",
 CellID->594665356,ExpressionUUID->"599300c3-8067-324a-0fa0-99ad31138090"],

Cell["One unnormalized run under plain noise, never renormalizing:", "Text",
 CellID->1466535282,ExpressionUUID->"499316cf-6a51-b537-7fa0-8fa90fe51c1d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"linearRun", "[", "seed_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"Fold", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"#1", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Knh", " ", ".", " ", "#1"}], " ", "step"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"cLin", " ", ".", " ", "#1"}], " ", "#2"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",",
        " ", "excited", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "step", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "steps"}], 
        "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[354]:=",
 CellID->5140989,ExpressionUUID->"2ee16f17-0b65-9d18-569e-8751ae11e462"],

Cell["Run four hundred of them:", "Text",
 CellID->1694956232,ExpressionUUID->"37a44649-1fc9-173d-5d5c-58139a7c7a07"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"linearStates", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"linearRun", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", "400", "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[355]:=",
 CellID->1547387255,ExpressionUUID->"7727b6f7-2c3c-391d-1edc-2fb145ce8867"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Average the unnormalized projectors, each already carrying its weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["w", "TI"], "=", "\[DoubleVerticalBar]", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleVerticalBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a1eaa68-7ffb-b035-2a25-4c32798f031f"],
 " in its trace, so no separate reweighting is applied:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1779178186,ExpressionUUID->"7b1e6369-8b0d-e6b2-2926-7b332eb9cc98"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"linearAverage", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "#", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
     " ", "linearStates"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[356]:=",
 CellID->1879667817,ExpressionUUID->"75aad74d-bf75-38f5-23a9-cf173a018adf"],

Cell["Measure the gap to the master equation:", "Text",
 CellID->1098063480,ExpressionUUID->"1c40da22-9bf5-6106-447f-d38c1d80306c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "@", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
    RowBox[{"linearAverage", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"evolve", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]lin", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "cLin", "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "excited", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"steps", " ", "step"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[357]:=",
 CellID->125264178,ExpressionUUID->"03b56da4-ec92-94f9-314a-84018524fec3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The unweighted reference-measure average lands on the master equation \
within Monte-Carlo scatter and Euler time-step error, the numerical face of \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\|01d53c", 
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "_"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dcedae6-c63c-0fd1-0bf5-d3c3f3c9553b"],
 ", reached with no pathwise renormalization."
}], "Text",
 CellID->812677712,ExpressionUUID->"027aacd9-8b9b-ca0d-3219-45832e2f9957"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the weight. The squared norm ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["w", "TI"], "=", 
   TemplateBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
    "BraKet"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "018fad51-cc5f-c6f3-37b4-451ae5ebacd9"],
 " is not conserved, and its own increment is where the likelihood sits. The \
non-Hermitian drift is built so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "+", 
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "792601a7-7c2e-1618-28dd-980175db7d62"],
 ", which cancels every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "422fa001-3abb-a233-73d4-3a6bbf4ff119"],
 " term in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "w"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d968898-757e-5b71-0bad-21c27c0b265b"],
 " and leaves the norm driven purely by the record,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->93844439,ExpressionUUID->"5c787eaa-3916-aaa9-0418-77f4b8a0f8f3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["w", "TI"], "=", 
    StyleBox["w", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["J", "TI"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["c", "TI"]]], "=", 
     RowBox[{"2", "\[ThinSpace]", 
      StyleBox["Re",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["Tr",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["[",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["c", "TI"]]}], 
       StyleBox["]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->243244218,ExpressionUUID->"321c9a0a-53e4-3b3a-6223-1c5465968600"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], "/", 
   StyleBox["w", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4556754e-32f3-38f6-736e-6d2846878adc"],
 " the normalized state. Under ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21d5e407-72d6-097c-57ea-fe6107635846"],
 " this drift-free increment makes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["w", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3df2759c-2159-6077-6b82-6cc650ec335d"],
 " a mean-one martingale, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\|01d53c", 
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["w", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1353847d-73f3-4ff8-4160-1e27058615c2"],
 ": exactly the statement that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["w", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["Q", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023adce6-f477-0954-33d9-d5c3fd025bbe"],
 " is a probability reweighting. Its logarithm accumulates the running \
log-likelihood,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->736003942,ExpressionUUID->"76eb59fc-b473-b7c5-1ee9-50a63d071d2f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["log",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["w", "TI"], "=", 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], "-", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->30476683,ExpressionUUID->"7dd80473-c718-e3dd-2be7-9e3cf292b127"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "climbing when a record increment aligns with the state's predicted signal \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["v", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0073a097-0f1d-653d-3000-39d1aaa84c07"],
 " and falling when it contradicts it. The finite seeded Euler sample of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["w", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "265272e3-db49-f23d-4e62-6bccdefdc107"],
 " should sit near one:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->57790923,ExpressionUUID->"4172bb43-7495-39b2-7701-332d7d218b98"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", 
    "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "linearStates"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[358]:=",
 CellID->1064275823,ExpressionUUID->"230bdc3d-d065-76ac-5108-d666e1105cf6"],

Cell["\<\
Different reference-noise histories carry different likelihood-ratio weights.\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->590249403,ExpressionUUID->"7083369b-c5f9-1da2-20b0-afc4f38c6788"],

Cell["Now visualize the distribution of their likelihood weights:", "Text",
 CellID->547939121,ExpressionUUID->"600ff364-211e-db59-1034-eb4e50a8a9a3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Histogram", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ",
      "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "linearStates"}], ",", " ", "30", ",", 
   " ", "\"\<PDF\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<likelihood-ratio weight dP/dQ\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<density\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<reference histories carry likelihood-ratio weights\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[359]:=",
 CellID->171228285,ExpressionUUID->"540b5a94-14ca-6d57-7c09-53de9d7f37bd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "These weights organize the section into a single identity. The unnormalized \
projector is the weighted normalized state, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], "=", 
   StyleBox["w", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0db8d008-2b7e-6047-3b47-ca524e0b32ad"],
 ", so the unweighted ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b5f3c3c-a0bd-b40a-4964-b679d1491f50"],
 "-average of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50e3ced9-efa3-8fb9-0090-e7828a57d583"],
 ", the weighted ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51e2478e-a4b0-4c7f-0792-5eebcd451745"],
 "-average of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7464e148-f188-b1ce-1c1b-f91580220314"],
 ", and the physical ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["P", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f8db726-7604-9df5-65b2-2e8003b6e7df"],
 "-average of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "22a876b6-5c8c-915d-52a8-6ff0553ee3a7"],
 " are one and the same master-equation state,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1578243061,ExpressionUUID->"38f0db08-93d0-aa19-688f-d352266af963"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\|01d53c", 
     StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThickSpace]", "=", "\[ThickSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox["\|01d53c", 
     StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["w", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["c", "TI"]]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThickSpace]", "=", "\[ThickSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox["\|01d53c", 
     StyleBox["P", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThickSpace]", "=", "\[ThickSpace]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "_"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1223164385,ExpressionUUID->"76285bca-be73-b625-1e28-52943b071d0f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The middle equality is the change of measure, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\|01d53c", 
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["w", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\|01d53c", 
    StyleBox["P", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e0bf47a-29b2-5087-4608-ee24484722ed"],
 " when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["w", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["Q", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b405c0d-64a5-b9f0-5970-56570d510bda"],
 ", and it is where the weight earns its keep. Drop it, average the same \
normalized states under ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ec9f25f-522a-b03f-26f6-f41967dc0305"],
 " with equal weight, and the result is not ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cabbcd0-b036-db9b-14a8-359dc1c0a9e1"],
 ", because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7549b383-d3bb-dea8-2376-2aece64fa4f2"],
 " draws records at the wrong physical frequencies. Put the three averages \
side by side at the final time:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->495355002,ExpressionUUID->"78c95527-fb77-4896-28f7-4c80fe021afc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ws", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], "]"}], 
        " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "linearStates"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"tildes", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "#", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
        " ", "linearStates"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"ref", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"evolve", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]lin", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "cLin", "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "excited", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"steps", " ", "step"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"rows", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<unnormalized projectors (Q)\>\"", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "tildes", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<likelihood-weighted (Q)\>\"", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Total", "[", "tildes", "]"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"Total", "[", "ws", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<equal-weight normalized (Q)\>\"", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
          RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"#1", "/", "#2"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"tildes", ",", " ", "ws"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
        "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"#", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
            RowBox[{"#", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
            "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"#", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "ref"}], ",", 
             " ", "\"\<Frobenius\>\""}], "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
         " ", "rows"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<reference-measure average\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<excited population\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<gap to master equation\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Alignment", " ", "->", " ", "Left"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[360]:=",
 CellID->1429172334,ExpressionUUID->"0e291a73-26c2-03ce-37d6-9c3d53775114"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two weighted rows sit on the master equation; the equal-weight row \
misses it, and by a bias no larger ensemble will close, since the error is in \
the sampling law and not the sample count. That gap is the whole content of \
the weight: it is what makes the reference measure physical. Two readings of \
one diffusive process follow from it: normalize the linear state and drive it \
with the physical innovation for the nonlinear state an experimenter tracks, \
or carry the unnormalized state under reference noise and keep its norm as \
the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["Q", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e50714f-9f2e-83ec-5660-69291ad8d136"],
 " factor."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1982316360,ExpressionUUID->"7fc38cd6-2f94-7c0b-25f0-25904a214751"],

Cell["\<\
One record carries both bookkeepings at once. Roll out a single linear run \
keeping its whole history:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1636237575,ExpressionUUID->"52bd9bab-8a7f-520d-0242-12f52f0a2157"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"linPathA5", "[", "seed_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"#1", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Knh", " ", ".", " ", "#1"}], " ", "step"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"cLin", " ", ".", " ", "#1"}], " ", "#2"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",",
        " ", "excited", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "step", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "steps"}], 
        "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[361]:=",
 CellID->1547648475,ExpressionUUID->"7fe6d50a-3e08-7026-259d-cd54bbbd430c"],

Cell["Take one such run for a fixed seed:", "Text",
 CellID->535623541,ExpressionUUID->"106f3a57-ec37-4f09-4014-bc1085c21253"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"oneA5", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"linPathA5", "[", "7", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[362]:=",
 CellID->464083887,ExpressionUUID->"5ce368aa-9e32-7f93-0490-81f41bc745f9"],

Cell["and its time grid:", "Text",
 CellID->1427425626,ExpressionUUID->"2409835b-76a2-7cb9-4c36-1b0503574683"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gridA5", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"step", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "steps"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[363]:=",
 CellID->689122476,ExpressionUUID->"55de0b04-0549-b416-03e5-a36eacfd1f7c"],

Cell["\<\
Read the two descriptions off that one run: the normalized state (the state \
direction the physical trajectory takes for this record) and the log-weight \
it accumulates (its running log-likelihood), side by side:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1284583753,ExpressionUUID->"12eebfc3-70f7-f40e-4295-36ad0083df54"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"gridA5", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "Z", 
                  " ", ".", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], " ", 
             "&"}], "[", 
            RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
           " ", "oneA5"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"steps", " ", "step"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "Medium"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<excited population (normalized)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      
      RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<the state you track\>\""}]}], 
     "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<  \>\"", ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"gridA5", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Log", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], 
             "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "oneA5"}]}], "}"}], 
       "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"steps", " ", "step"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "All"}], 
        "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "Medium"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<log weight  log ||psi||^2\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
      "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<the likelihood it carries\>\""}]}], 
     "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[364]:=",
 CellID->1229478228,ExpressionUUID->"5725d6ca-0b7f-1acb-7eda-cf94ae0a6811"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same record has a normalized-state reading and a running weight. The \
normalized state is the physical trajectory an experimenter tracks; the \
weight is the extra likelihood factor, needed only to turn averages taken \
under the reference measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70ead02b-38d1-354c-20e9-ca75b9659f96"],
 " into physical ones."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1956186523,ExpressionUUID->"09d7f5ce-7f21-c26a-3fec-eca87ad590b0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The catch of the linear method is that the weights spread, so a handful of \
records come to dominate the average, the importance-sampling degeneracy. \
Measure it with the effective sample size ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["N", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["eff",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Sum]",
       FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
      StyleBox["w", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["\[Sum]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["w", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "229972e4-7d0e-897c-52a7-6bce74b8d846"],
 ". Run an ensemble of linear paths:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1104760091,ExpressionUUID->"21fb93d6-8bae-9e34-5798-0a902e58e51e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"essPathsA5", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"linPathA5", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", "400", "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[365]:=",
 CellID->283765075,ExpressionUUID->"239269fa-bed2-0e72-51a1-80a43b675558"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Read ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["N", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["eff",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "/", 
   StyleBox["N", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "141dc450-8fbb-3551-3c22-de1a2a4f9fbb"],
 " from the squared-norm weights at sampled times:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1844722010,ExpressionUUID->"33f465a2-c944-5788-618c-7c0fe8f13dd2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"essA5", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"w", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], 
               "]"}], " ", "&"}], "@", 
             RowBox[{"#", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "j", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
          " ", "essPathsA5"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Total", "[", "w", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
           RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "400."}]}], "]"}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"steps", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "20"}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[366]:=",
 CellID->1051270324,ExpressionUUID->"6ae608ed-420f-d8e0-1a9d-a1b777bbaaca"],

Cell["and plot its decay over time:", "Text",
 CellID->152418458,ExpressionUUID->"7456dc60-8a8d-205f-1c6d-d64a2f3872a5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"gridA5", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", ";;", " ", "20"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
      " ", "essA5"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<effective sample size / N\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<the linear weights degenerate: fewer records carry the \
average\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[367]:=",
 CellID->1026990147,ExpressionUUID->"7cf7943f-295e-114d-248c-0e7948eb6397"],

Cell["\<\
The effective fraction falls from one toward a fraction of the ensemble: as \
time goes on, the unweighted linear average is carried by ever fewer \
high-weight records, and its Monte-Carlo error grows even though it remains \
unbiased. That is the price of the linear picture's convenience, and the \
reason the nonlinear (renormalized) equation, which keeps every trajectory \
equally weighted, is what a long real-time filter uses.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1165560109,ExpressionUUID->"186d7224-6ee6-971a-4813-6b8e0a90fa60"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The Driven Atom, Averaged and Watched", "Subsection",
 CellID->866904439,ExpressionUUID->"28783f79-c8ba-30ce-5807-b722e94c8214"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The problem.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " One driven, damped, emitting atom, carried in full generality and then \
watched three ways. Its unconditional master equation keeps detuning, a \
thermal drive, and pure dephasing together,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1332589990,ExpressionUUID->"6369cf55-7e98-45e5-1116-e71f7b2d2fcf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", "1"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
        StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}], "2"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["z", "TI"]]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1878932146,ExpressionUUID->"695e18f7-9077-7daa-1f65-91b1210247f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "and relaxes to a mixed steady state inside the ball. Three separate \
environmental channels carry information away, one dissipator each: the \
downward channel ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], "\[DownArrow]"], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", "1"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01025a43-78b1-6e71-3732-5c2d7944355b"],
 " is excited-to-ground emission, the upward channel ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], "\[UpArrow]"], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "45a2a882-eb03-e595-7351-41ef8eb7cfff"],
 " is thermal absorption from the bath, and the dephasing channel ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"]]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1bf7f187-9eae-ffe3-498c-e8e11b58c5c9"],
 " scrambles the phase while moving no population. Detuning is different in \
kind: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}], "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10512a4e-e651-dddd-406e-cc2b93e5a727"],
 " is Hamiltonian, so it turns the state without opening a fourth channel and \
without mixing it. We hold all three channels active throughout and vary only \
how much of their output the observer keeps: nothing, the fluorescence alone, \
or all three ideally. These are three levels of knowledge about one atom, not \
three physical models, running from the mixed interior point (no record) \
through mixed conditioned states (partial record) to pure conditioned states \
(complete record), every one sharing the single unconditional average ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\|01d53c", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5176ba42-8596-944f-070d-3c2c2c20fe95"],
 ". Heterodyne split one emitted field into two quadratures; here three \
distinct mechanisms carry three independent records, and the question is how \
many of them the observer keeps."
}], "Text",
 CellID->81974322,ExpressionUUID->"6ab79099-cfc9-41ff-1a4c-09c2ea7c13c5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Start with the level we never record, the unconditional steady state, the \
mixed point every watched trajectory below will circle. Two rates organize \
it: the longitudinal rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "1"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cff0d2a-0962-39b9-4484-a574a8148b83"],
 " at which populations relax, and the transverse rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2"], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "1"], "+", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ecbc277-6fbb-da5a-06c8-e4310a4fa8a0"],
 " at which coherences decay, faster than ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "1"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "457cd362-8cff-9a44-7303-cb4c248be8ae"],
 " by the extra dephasing. Define the steady Bloch vector in closed form:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->101329809,ExpressionUUID->"1130cedf-2841-d5f7-40cf-e79949f5bfdd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"steadyGeneral", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[CapitalDelta]_", ",", " ", "\[CapitalOmega]_", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]_", ",",
      " ", "nT_", ",", " ", "kd_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"G1", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "nT"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"G2", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"2", " ", "nT"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "/", 
           "2"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Gamma]", " ", "kd"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"den", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"G1", " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"G2", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
          
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "^", "2"}], " ", "G2"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "\[Gamma]"}], " ", "\[CapitalOmega]", " ", 
           "\[CapitalDelta]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", " ", "\[CapitalOmega]", " ", "G2"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "\[Gamma]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"G2", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}], "/", 
        "den"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[368]:=",
 CellID->122926644,ExpressionUUID->"3468d219-8f65-5d49-5c17-d4432a102793"],

Cell["\<\
Check it against the toolkit's steady-state finder with detuning, \
temperature, and dephasing all switched on:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->827648486,ExpressionUUID->"07018e41-afaf-9e12-2d3e-202aca5be578"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"steadyGeneral", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "1.3", ",", " ", "3.", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "0.4", ",", " ", 
      "0.25"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
     RowBox[{"First", "@", 
      RowBox[{"stationary", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"1.3", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "Z"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"3.", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"1.", " ", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"0.4", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
           "lower"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"1.", " ", "0.4"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "lower", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"1.", " ", "0.25"}], "]"}], " ", "Z"}]}], "}"}]}], 
       "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[369]:=",
 CellID->785423779,ExpressionUUID->"429ca171-278a-9358-72a3-393b523ce1a2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The discrepancy is at numerical precision: the closed form is exact for the \
stated finite-dimensional Bloch equations. The detuning enters through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2", "2"], "+", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2265709e-c6e2-934c-521b-69dbf294e196"],
 " in the denominator, so the resonance has a Lorentzian denominator of width \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c2451d3-5dad-cf90-05dc-489d545995fa"],
 " that the drive power-broadens through the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fb71b50-5b0e-8f73-254c-931a5eb8d259"],
 " term; temperature lifts the ground-state bias, since at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "389fd111-b284-1b04-68a4-c95ac731666e"],
 " the state rests at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["eq",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", "-", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a68dc76-92bd-40cf-2a17-d63027481215"],
 " rather than the south pole. Plot the steady excited population ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "+", 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1373306a-3754-8710-4100-aa3442e6ea7a"],
 " against detuning, weak drive against strong:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1525499759,ExpressionUUID->"2f521ae3-0d3c-4250-5561-93cda4c910ba"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"d", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"steadyGeneral", "[", 
              RowBox[{
              "d", ",", " ", "om", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
               "0."}], "]"}], "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"d", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "8"}], ",", " ", "8", ",", " ", "0.05"}], "}"}]}], 
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"om", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "4."}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<\[CapitalOmega] = 1\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<\[CapitalOmega] = 4\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<detuning \[CapitalDelta]\[Omega]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<steady excited population\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<resonance is a power-broadened Lorentzian in detuning\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[370]:=",
 CellID->1068945273,ExpressionUUID->"2fdf34a4-4672-e0d0-55e4-ad0e7304b23a"],

Cell["\<\
The excited population peaks on resonance and falls off as a Lorentzian to \
either side; the stronger drive both lifts the peak toward saturation at one \
half and widens it, the power broadening. That is the general averaged atom, \
the no-record level: with the detector ignored, the state relaxes \
deterministically to one mixed interior point. To watch it we must say what a \
detector does with each of the three outputs, and that choice, not the \
Liouvillian, is what picks a trajectory out of the average.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->753001716,ExpressionUUID->"4de787d6-2024-7dd3-7b9c-1e9051d14739"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the same atom, watched. Fix the drive ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55fa1cea-4458-dcd2-0399-95b46dd2a638"],
 ", the decay rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5117b661-6297-dae6-072c-284b1723a8cc"],
 ", the detuning ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4874a11a-0b78-4cc4-780b-3944ae0d162e"],
 ", the bath occupation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e1748f8-0734-d73c-262d-61a2b2c6ba06"],
 ", and the dephasing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e2b9108-d4ae-d6a1-4628-0955dd58bc8b"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->233751987,ExpressionUUID->"59b55f82-b518-72dd-0f4b-56ec3cad4027"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]dr", " ", "=", " ", "3."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]dr", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]dr", " ", "=", " ", "0.8"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"nTdr", " ", "=", " ", "0.3"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"kdDr", " ", "=", " ", "0.2"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[371]:=",
 CellID->688983072,ExpressionUUID->"1410ebbc-cc48-afc5-3c2f-02f9e5e2f52f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build the Hamiltonian, a detuning about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b4a9728-6877-44ef-3949-0f7209022e35"],
 " plus a drive about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d9cae35-b3ea-e9a2-6ba3-407ec59cbb88"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1379778257,ExpressionUUID->"47ae793e-1388-a017-6d56-7178a622f37d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Hdr", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]dr", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "Z"}], " ", "+", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]dr", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[372]:=",
 CellID->1425464440,ExpressionUUID->"0718ed2d-1535-5ad4-2d27-05779cc0283e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build the three channel operators from the toolkit's ",
 Cell[BoxData["lower"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "372f13ab-79ee-7986-5ed4-8af57f9b4bec"],
 ": emission down, thermal absorption up, and dephasing about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c367b34-bfe1-5d6f-15ce-737e399427b5"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->939350965,ExpressionUUID->"75911979-a02e-ddea-23ae-9122d1d8a730"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Rdown", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]dr", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"nTdr", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", "lower"}]}],
   ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Rup", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]dr", " ", "nTdr"}], "]"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "lower", "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Rphi", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]dr", " ", "kdDr"}], "]"}], " ", "Z"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[373]:=",
 CellID->619140003,ExpressionUUID->"0dec446f-046e-4336-3b94-5e49ad1b2e1c"],

Cell["Collect the three as the leak list:", "Text",
 CellID->266834637,ExpressionUUID->"75dc925b-5bf3-f22e-23e3-14055d87c174"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"drLeaks", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"Rdown", ",", " ", "Rup", ",", " ", "Rphi"}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[374]:=",
 CellID->1001517655,ExpressionUUID->"03e98152-a240-0eaa-3196-191fd7f554f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With the detector ignored, the state relaxes to the mixed interior point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
   StyleBox["ss",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a00be71-6857-3e36-2a3f-303b09e3851c"],
 " of the closed form above; read its length, which a pure state would carry \
as one:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->39808583,ExpressionUUID->"1b61afbf-df52-1398-491e-46f8dae761e2"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"settled", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"steadyGeneral", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[CapitalDelta]dr", ",", " ", "\[CapitalOmega]dr", ",", " ", 
     "\[Gamma]dr", ",", " ", "nTdr", ",", " ", "kdDr"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Norm", "[", "settled", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[375]:=",
 CellID->81581324,ExpressionUUID->"54cfcfa8-25f2-71dd-7cf4-e6f253874327"],

Cell["\<\
Well short of one: with no record kept, the atom is mixed, sitting inside the \
ball where drive, emission, thermal absorption, and dephasing balance.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->671164176,ExpressionUUID->"4c7b9ae5-550e-b845-7418-13cf5cb80aaf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To watch it, we must put a detector on each output, and that choice, not ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[ScriptCapitalL]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71e2106e-13a9-e35f-2791-8a48a65db1a5"],
 ", is what selects a trajectory. Read all three channels by phase-zero \
homodyne, each carrying its own independent noise ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5fb5a314-14a9-f5fc-054a-3b5e9d5ddfc6"],
 " (with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}], "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4caa88fa-f24e-a9d3-74a9-21a787f8fb39"],
 "), so each record is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "+", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "781e04d5-949b-4939-2825-9d9f1d2e1803"],
 ". Which system observable does each carry? Since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "030eefb9-536c-2ae9-3135-06e366197833"],
 ", both emission records track ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13b93a61-4b06-9a06-4146-bc4b6eb0e96c"],
 ", differing only by their thermal weights, while the dephasing operator is \
Hermitian, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "+", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "=", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"]]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "700a2ccf-4fe7-b0c9-2009-c5a969930213"],
 " and its record tracks ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "140d84d1-9e60-51c0-3c32-1d9b1b15232a"],
 ". Confirm the three record drifts are exactly those combinations:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->374148378,ExpressionUUID->"4f0947a0-1196-40ba-7537-5e0aa0231280"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"probe", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"0.5", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"0.5", " ", "I"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "probe", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
         RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"#", " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", ".",
            " ", "probe"}], "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"Rdown", ",", " ", "Rup", ",", " ", "Rphi"}], "}"}]}], ")"}], 
     " ", "-", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[Gamma]dr", " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"nTdr", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"a", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[Gamma]dr", " ", "nTdr"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"a", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[Gamma]dr", " ", "kdDr"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"a", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[377]:=",
 CellID->2126328594,ExpressionUUID->"248a8160-2ca3-5e04-4c89-194a4556256e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Zero in every slot: three independent records collapse onto two system \
observables. Two different baths both report ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26ed9998-8884-b223-4e92-10c229360109"],
 ", one reports ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ac06e6b-f116-7b59-0aff-803480a349a3"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65a717e6-c8c5-b5f7-135c-8ec3e9711fdd"],
 ", generally nonzero, appears in no record at all; it reaches the \
conditioned state only through the Hamiltonian rotation. Channel identity and \
measured observable are not the same thing."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1152367211,ExpressionUUID->"3ab59720-208d-140d-6a4a-0e8a51387f57"],

Cell["\<\
Integrate the record-blind master equation once, the baseline every ensemble \
must return to:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->599499195,ExpressionUUID->"75579e92-42ca-6d62-236c-17dc777f3448"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"refRun", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"evolveODE", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Hdr", ",", " ", "drLeaks", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "excited", "]"}], ",", " ", "8."}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[378]:=",
 CellID->477283400,ExpressionUUID->"2e55f28b-4749-0e5a-566a-ebd572fc54a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Run one conditioned history that keeps only the fluorescence, watching ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], "\[DownArrow]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "396a2699-bf3c-f954-6f69-bfc33acecbbe"],
 " while the thermal-absorption and dephasing outputs escape:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->449610334,ExpressionUUID->"1bb23a02-0434-56a9-4941-bc6cadc13cf3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"watchedOne", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "excited", "]"}], ",", " ", "Hdr", ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "Rdown", "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"Rup", ",", " ", "Rphi"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "0.01", ",", " ", 
     "8.", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[379]:=",
 CellID->1143962738,ExpressionUUID->"0443f7da-681a-ff36-2c70-ee8409acc21c"],

Cell["Run another that keeps all three channels ideally:", "Text",
 CellID->1043470919,ExpressionUUID->"4e7b0eee-1e32-42cf-7618-a7c89bc71015"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"watchedAll", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "excited", "]"}], ",", " ", "Hdr", ",", 
     " ", "drLeaks", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "0.01", ",", " ", "8.", ",", " ", "5"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[380]:=",
 CellID->505712527,ExpressionUUID->"0029b61e-e057-a799-31d6-285b91e30de3"],

Cell["Take the shared time grid off that run:", "Text",
 CellID->1677321332,ExpressionUUID->"4d6d3611-50e6-56f1-7b12-a85b60933cdb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"whenDr", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"watchedAll", "[", "\"\<times\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[381]:=",
 CellID->1181455231,ExpressionUUID->"29e2b788-3fef-f960-5f91-2ed2b99bc84a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The fluorescence-only history obeys ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "=", "\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", "\[ScriptCapitalH]", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], "\[DownArrow]"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "\[DownArrow]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03070159-0ba8-dd63-313c-9903ae42a449"],
 ": the unwatched channels stay in ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[ScriptCapitalL]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21ec52ec-14ad-8ff7-5794-4bb69d59d5dd"],
 " but condition nothing. Read the smallest purity each run reaches:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->805377406,ExpressionUUID->"10dc93f3-40fa-a76c-40e3-0abd708c0db6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
    RowBox[{"purity", " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"watchedOne", "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
    RowBox[{"purity", " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"watchedAll", "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[382]:=",
 CellID->728305703,ExpressionUUID->"0c8eb1fd-23df-bcec-34b5-28a7566b0636"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The fluorescence-only run drops well below one, genuinely mixed; the fully \
watched run holds at one. Temperature and dephasing are equally present in \
both, active in the same ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[ScriptCapitalL]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15af50f1-da00-725d-4355-49badfb540a7"],
 "; the only difference is whether their information is collected. Missing \
two of the three channels mixes the conditioned state; catching all three \
keeps it pure, thermal drive and dephasing notwithstanding. That is the \
sharper form of \"watching keeps purity\": not watching anything, but holding \
a complete ideal record of every channel that carries information away."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2004076868,ExpressionUUID->"0fd09d21-d637-448f-35ef-148ae3c22ed5"],

Cell["\<\
See it as three curves in time, the record-blind purity against the two \
conditioned runs:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->893892827,ExpressionUUID->"2d58e4db-fdb8-3fff-5b67-fd84f43285c5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"whenDr", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"purity", "[", 
           RowBox[{"refRun", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
         " ", "whenDr"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"whenDr", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"purity", " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"watchedOne", "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}],
      ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"whenDr", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"purity", " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"watchedAll", "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], 
      "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<no record (unconditional)\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<fluorescence only\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<all three channels\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", "1.1"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<purity\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<only the complete record keeps a conditioned run pure\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.996853203650015*^9, 3.996853239646068*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[409]:=",
 CellID->430036832,ExpressionUUID->"5331d2da-71bb-e99d-02ce-cb84004fbbe7"],

Cell["\<\
The unconditional purity slides smoothly from one to its mixed steady value; \
the fluorescence-only run jitters below it, genuinely mixed; the fully \
watched run rides the top at one. Purity is a property of the record kept, \
not of the atom. The same three levels read on the Bloch sphere, the pure \
surface path and the mixed interior path circling the one record-blind steady \
point:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->114465421,ExpressionUUID->"43630a3a-ab57-6174-7110-ac67cee2305e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"blochPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"watchedAll", "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"watchedOne", "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", "\"\<complete record stays on the surface; fluorescence only \
wanders inside\>\"", ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<all three channels (pure)\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<fluorescence only (mixed)\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"Black", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PointSize", "[", "0.035", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Point", "[", "settled", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[384]:=",
 CellID->609955738,ExpressionUUID->"1026404a-81cf-d4cd-41de-5a14307bbe17"],

Cell["\<\
The fully watched trajectory stays on the surface, pure, circling the black \
interior point; the fluorescence-only trajectory wanders through the \
interior, mixed. Both must average back to that same black point, the atom \
with no record at all. Check it: build an ensemble of each monitoring and \
compare its mean to the unconditional reference:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->465296703,ExpressionUUID->"74202e85-faa6-6568-1ddf-c7eeff534fb2"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"crowdOne", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "excited", "]"}], ",", " ", "Hdr", ",", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "Rdown", "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"Rup", ",", " ", "Rphi"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "0.01", ",", " ",
         "8.", ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "100"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"crowdAll", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "excited", "]"}], ",", " ", "Hdr", ",", 
        " ", "drLeaks", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "0.01", ",", " ", "8.", ",", " ", "k"}],
        "]"}], "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "100"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"ref", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"refRun", " ", "/@", " ", "whenDr"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
      RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"#1", " ", "-", " ", "#2"}], ",", 
           " ", "\"\<Frobenius\>\""}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "crowdOne", "]"}], ",", " ", "ref"}], "}"}]}], 
       "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
      RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"#1", " ", "-", " ", "#2"}], ",", 
           " ", "\"\<Frobenius\>\""}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "crowdAll", "]"}], ",", " ", "ref"}], "}"}]}], 
       "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[385]:=",
 CellID->340301607,ExpressionUUID->"2d7e3b6d-b319-8b08-5b05-b336c6add652"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both gaps sit at the hundred-trajectory sampling level: averaging the \
record away returns the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5a40a2e0-989c-e39d-0a7f-3bca192eb1e7"],
 " whether the conditioned states were mixed or pure. The two knobs from the \
toolkit still set the residue, more trajectories against the scatter and a \
finer step against the bias."
}], "Text",
 CellID->730813709,ExpressionUUID->"70f38dee-376a-4447-2080-24c8421f2ead"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One honest caveat on the pure fully watched run. Writing the thermal bath \
as the two operators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", "1"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2824dbec-c043-5d14-59db-d2c9f1f6247e"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23171ab6-4dff-4f28-512c-93f06b8a1272"],
 " dilates it into two effective vacuum channels, and monitoring both of \
those is what keeps the trajectory pure. A real thermal reservoir is itself \
mixed, and ordinary access to its physical output need not deliver the two \
clean records this idealization assumes. Complete monitoring of all three \
effective channels is an information-complete unravelling: it shows what full \
environmental knowledge would imply, not necessarily what a laboratory \
detector on a warm bath can reach."
}], "Text",
 CellID->939888283,ExpressionUUID->"285991ce-1a51-dc0e-5866-08a89fe5a754"],

Cell["\<\
So one Liouvillian carries three answers. The black interior point is the \
atom with the record thrown away; the interior stochastic path is the same \
atom watched incompletely; the surface stochastic path is the atom watched in \
full. None is more true than the others, and all three average to the first: \
they answer three different questions about one open system.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->504741409,ExpressionUUID->"1447630d-e4f1-bc17-3c7d-7b568c85077d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The Mollow Triplet: Resonance-Fluorescence Spectrum", "Subsection",
 CellID->1085488748,ExpressionUUID->"2eb894ff-d8e2-f9b5-5647-0db8d894cb9f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The problem.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The spectrum (power spectrum) of the light a driven atom emits, computed \
by quantum regression from the two-time correlations of the master equation. \
The atom is the resonant emitter of the previous section,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2053363947,ExpressionUUID->"6e0b0981-7bde-7e15-1608-a0eb7e6b457f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "."], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->865306486,ExpressionUUID->"7d43776d-a0a0-3956-2b71-6f36d15a8bbc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its light divides into two parts: an ",
 StyleBox["elastic", "TI"],
 " (coherent) line at the drive frequency, a delta function carrying the \
weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      SubscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        SubscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
        StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
       StyleBox["ss",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "215fa697-6eb8-710a-5764-3fd10b4d4050"],
 ", and the ",
 StyleBox["inelastic", "TI"],
 " (fluorescence) spectrum of the fluctuations ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["ss",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c8b361a-878c-2404-3488-a844323e8f6e"],
 ", given by quantum regression as the steady-state correlation"
}], "Text",
 CellID->480044997,ExpressionUUID->"4bb231e2-5836-31a9-7941-a8cc59c083f3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["inel",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[Proportional]", 
    StyleBox["Re",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["ss",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->829253909,ExpressionUUID->"6e392069-461f-3828-17c6-ba3373ab8b72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Regression runs this correlation on the same Liouvillian ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[ScriptCapitalL]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43052563-9173-3450-713a-bd4d20079eba"],
 " that evolves the state, so Fourier transform turns the propagator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "44a4da74-fa22-10cf-6c5b-dc31ffd76215"],
 " into the resolvent ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "-", "\[ScriptCapitalL]"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b3641f4-0f52-42c0-0ace-58beaae7102a"],
 ". For weak driving the inelastic part is a single line; for strong driving ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", ">", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4be4e521-e77f-ec2d-799b-fc8a920bb777"],
 " it splits into the three-peaked ",
 StyleBox["Mollow triplet", "TI"],
 ", a central line and two sidebands at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20bfa7a2-79b2-80c7-5044-3e0c7844d22d"],
 ", the dynamical Stark effect."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1633538843,ExpressionUUID->"55f244d6-d311-02bf-0382-5d93e6a45085"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Homodyne detection instead reads a chosen quadrature, and its spectrum can \
dip ",
 StyleBox["below", "TI"],
 " the shot-noise floor: squeezed, nonclassical light. Build both from the \
same big matrix."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1582554316,ExpressionUUID->"7b67ca56-f022-f422-291c-ec1381d4df08"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One last set of quantities from the master equation, all through the \
eigen-based spectrum tool built for the quantum point contact (",
 Cell[BoxData["regressionSpectrum"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d812222-80c8-810b-5bbe-bb8c3162d051"],
 "). It needs no shifted frequency grid, because the steady mode is dropped \
explicitly. The inelastic fluorescence spectrum is its correlation of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3ce1a32f-562f-710d-649e-3a8963da4057"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1433588095,ExpressionUUID->"300dd36f-3764-9e2b-6032-cb494216e571"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"mollowInelastic", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]_", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]_", ",", " ", "tones_"}], 
    "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"big", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"liouvillian", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]", "]"}], " ", "lower"}], "}"}], ",",
           " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"rss", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"First", "@", 
         RowBox[{"stationary", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]", "]"}], " ", "lower"}], "}"}]}], 
          "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"dm", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"lower", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
            RowBox[{"lower", " ", ".", " ", "rss"}], "]"}], " ", "id2"}]}]}], 
        "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"regressionSpectrum", "[", 
        RowBox[{"big", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"dm", " ", ".", " ", "rss"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "dm", "]"}], ",", " ", "tones"}], 
        "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[388]:=",
 CellID->659120451,ExpressionUUID->"4c3da1d2-94cd-5311-75c2-389c1d783e7b"],

Cell["\<\
Sweep frequencies (centered on zero, no offset needed) for a weak and a \
strong drive:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1530466570,ExpressionUUID->"6725d2c7-83c3-a466-0eda-cba136770f4c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tones", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "9"}], ",", " ", "9", ",", " ", "0.05"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"weak", ",", " ", "strong"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"mollowInelastic", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0.6", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "tones"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"mollowInelastic", "[", 
      RowBox[{"6.", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "tones"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[389]:=",
 CellID->1148538709,ExpressionUUID->"30f7e14b-6bce-fb20-608c-f9150e78c60a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Weakly driven, the inelastic spectrum is a single line at the drive \
frequency. Strongly driven, it splits into the ",
 StyleBox["Mollow triplet",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": a central line and two sidebands at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36b60ac5-0872-487b-5e4d-a3afa9071b41"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1755752829,ExpressionUUID->"42a6af43-9231-5484-725d-472d27c43eee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now visualize the weak- and strong-drive inelastic spectra together. Their \
absolute scales differ by orders of magnitude (the weak line would vanish on \
the strong axis), so plot each normalized to its own peak to compare the ",
 StyleBox["shapes", "TI"],
 ", a single line against the triplet:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1464413666,ExpressionUUID->"2cbe9beb-23d5-e081-5445-12b55661b2eb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tones", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"weak", "/", 
         RowBox[{"Max", "[", "weak", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tones", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"strong", "/", 
         RowBox[{"Max", "[", "strong", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "6"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      "None"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<weak drive\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<strong drive\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<frequency (relative to drive)\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<inelastic spectrum (each / its peak)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<strong driving splits the inelastic spectrum into the Mollow \
triplet\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[391]:=",
 CellID->477976485,ExpressionUUID->"0e2217e0-2499-112c-37d1-8eca4d2c6076"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The sidebands sit near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ff6f087-faf0-a568-158d-e9e0fe8a0fb2"],
 ": under strong driving the atom's levels are dressed into a four-level \
ladder, whose transitions produce the three lines. Confirm the sidebands land \
at the drive strength:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1079844684,ExpressionUUID->"16ade48a-ef31-1f64-3e52-fdd78ac4624e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"tones", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"FindPeaks", "[", "strong", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "6"}], "]"}], " ", "<", 
     " ", "0.6"}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[392]:=",
 CellID->681181479,ExpressionUUID->"00277703-eb91-13ac-31dd-6f6c8e2461f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The peaks sit at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "733a2e46-5515-03a9-22d9-c0205ca051f3"],
 ". Confirm too that the inelastic spectrum is nowhere negative, as a genuine \
power spectrum must be:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1509583139,ExpressionUUID->"3a85de0d-f49a-8910-6aba-d056fd2cd87a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Min", "[", "strong", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[393]:=",
 CellID->1635716693,ExpressionUUID->"51a44dbe-e8d5-ad1e-075c-64fb8961f464"],

Cell["Nonnegative within numerical precision.", "Text",
 CellID->677984635,ExpressionUUID->"48fac1ee-cedf-3fa9-7899-d8cbeb6b85f3"],

Cell["\<\
The elastic line lives separately, a delta at zero frequency whose weight is \
the coherent dipole; it dominates at weak drive and all but vanishes at \
strong drive as the light turns fully inelastic:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->328233113,ExpressionUUID->"57d65f39-cbd6-cc34-7dee-5762ee60971e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"elasticWeight", "[", "\[CapitalOmega]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"rss", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"First", "@", 
        RowBox[{"stationary", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "1.", "]"}], " ", "lower"}], "}"}]}], 
         "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
        RowBox[{"lower", " ", ".", " ", "rss"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[394]:=",
 CellID->1783463389,ExpressionUUID->"2f9472dd-9541-0a0e-55ac-6b871cf45954"],

Cell["At weak drive the coherent weight is substantial:", "Text",
 CellID->345427966,ExpressionUUID->"3d3a3c62-0210-a9d6-64d9-b64cb7aafb3c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"elasticWeight", "[", "0.6", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[395]:=",
 CellID->438183996,ExpressionUUID->"357989b9-a09f-e5cf-6306-20e2d12bcf15"],

Cell["and at strong drive it all but vanishes:", "Text",
 CellID->1914081905,ExpressionUUID->"0fae0884-bf9b-3b68-3555-a1ee3a2f89b2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"elasticWeight", "[", "6.", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[396]:=",
 CellID->2065968196,ExpressionUUID->"33445fcf-b4d7-bfdc-617c-56a93d630526"],

Cell["\<\
The coherent weight falls by more than an order of magnitude from weak to \
strong drive. To watch the triplet being born, sweep the drive continuously:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1331494444,ExpressionUUID->"7ca36f6b-0429-ee44-2450-8735adddb4ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mollowDrives", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0.3", ",", " ", "8", ",", " ", "0.25"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[397]:=",
 CellID->785021954,ExpressionUUID->"18db0f17-f9d7-aea7-48f8-a750f863f48d"],

Cell["\<\
Stack the inelastic spectra into a heatmap, each row scaled to its own peak \
so the sidebands stay visible against the central peak that dwarfs them:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1114713077,ExpressionUUID->"73df1c92-0fac-0f76-21e4-95dcaa59525c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mollowHeat", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"#", "/", 
       RowBox[{"Max", "[", "#", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"mollowInelastic", "[", 
        RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "11"}], ",", " ", "11", ",", " ", "0.1"}], "]"}]}], 
        "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "mollowDrives"}], ")"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[398]:=",
 CellID->1422334928,ExpressionUUID->"5656aae2-2851-4b0a-7e6d-43cc49e41650"],

Cell["\<\
Plot it as a heatmap, weak drive at the bottom rising to strong at the top:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1250368603,ExpressionUUID->"30301fc7-228d-22ca-61cf-96a157387010"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ArrayPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"mollowHeat", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DataReversed", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ColorFunction", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<SunsetColors\>\""}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<frequency\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<drive \[CapitalOmega]\>\""}],
      "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<the Mollow triplet is born as the drive grows (rows scaled to \
peak)\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[399]:=",
 CellID->378185340,ExpressionUUID->"27fbb2ba-f259-6eaf-4d98-2be787ec34f5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bright ridge splits into three, the outer two fanning apart as the \
drive grows: the dressed-state sidebands at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "=", "\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "61fb7f33-6b9b-fc5f-1799-777d0e2fc6a5"],
 ". The triplet is what an ordinary spectrometer sees."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1232642540,ExpressionUUID->"0649aad6-fad6-6687-2e76-4393ff634ced"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A homodyne detector sees something an intensity spectrometer cannot: it \
measures one quadrature ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"i", "\[Theta]"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d47e9ac-fa3d-7380-6b7c-0009ffc841ea"],
 ", and its spectrum, normalized so the shot-noise floor is one, can fall \
below that floor. The weak drive we examine, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d029a07-fcbf-4406-2b31-1c60f54a2f6c"],
 ", is exactly an exceptional point of this Liouvillian, the same coalescence \
the quantum point contact met: its two dressed modes merge there, so we read \
this spectrum with the mode-free ",
 Cell[BoxData["resolventSpectrum"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "59984c08-f847-9374-0fb8-6655f9f3fe5e"],
 " rather than the eigenmode sum, which would divide by a singular \
eigenbasis. Build it from the measurement current fluctuations:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1959721910,ExpressionUUID->"5dc87cf5-1cff-6993-0bc8-75bf948a3bf9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"mollowHom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[CapitalOmega]_", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]_", ",", " ", "\[Theta]_", ",", 
     " ", "tones_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"c", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]", "]"}], " ", "lower"}]}], ",", " ", 
       "big", ",", " ", "rss", ",", " ", "cth", ",", " ", "mq", ",", " ", 
       "mean"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"big", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"liouvillian", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "c", "}"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"rss", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"First", "@", 
        RowBox[{"stationary", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", "c", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"cth", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"c", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "\[Theta]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"mq", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"cth", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "cth", "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"mean", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{"mq", " ", ".", " ", "rss"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"resolventSpectrum", "[", 
        RowBox[{"big", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"cth", " ", ".", " ", "rss"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"rss", " ", ".", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "cth", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"mean", " ", "rss"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"mq", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"mean", " ", "id2"}]}], ",", " ", "tones"}], "]"}]}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[400]:=",
 CellID->1867364171,ExpressionUUID->"11c4d396-5bb6-ac17-47fb-cad05e40f77d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At weak drive, one quadrature is squeezed and the perpendicular one is not. \
Compare the two at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "=", "0.25", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a630626-6fcf-04f9-7a10-9f800a7a6ec3"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1544748084,ExpressionUUID->"145a40c7-d93c-08fa-3c7a-59a0d8c95ac0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tones", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"mollowHom", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0.25", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "tones"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tones", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"mollowHom", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0.25", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "tones"}], 
         "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<squeezed quadrature (\[Theta] = \[Pi]/2)\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<anti-squeezed (\[Theta] = 0)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0.7", ",", " ", "All"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<frequency\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<homodyne spectrum / shot noise\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<resonance fluorescence dips below the shot-noise floor\>\""}]}],
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9968531365899773`*^9, 3.9968531406575613`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[406]:=",
 CellID->1622069726,ExpressionUUID->"4bf1d662-0ef6-65a6-798e-c84caa834f8c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1628b50c-bf07-7ea3-3fd7-2d563ab24489"],
 " quadrature dips below the dashed shot-noise line while its partner rises \
above it: the atom's fluorescence is squeezed, its noise pushed below the \
vacuum in one quadrature at the cost of excess in the other. Confirm the dip \
is real:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->137201459,ExpressionUUID->"2f4039c6-41c1-f8a2-557f-b0a07075ca88"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
  RowBox[{"mollowHom", "[", 
   RowBox[{"0.25", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "tones"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[402]:=",
 CellID->1509753751,ExpressionUUID->"7ea6321c-88b1-0c83-265d-b446294456e9"],

Cell["\<\
Below one: sub-shot-noise, a signature of nonclassical light that only \
phase-sensitive (homodyne) detection can reveal, and that the \
necessarily-nonnegative intensity spectrum of the triplet can never show.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1992991547,ExpressionUUID->"2eba4b4c-086b-ae59-565a-6316a91ff4a3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How far the squeezing reaches, and where it is deepest, is a question about \
the drive, and it is cleanest at zero frequency, the bottom of the dip we \
just drew. There the homodyne spectrum has the closed form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "1", "+", "8", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"1", "+", "2", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "3"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b0563d8-53c7-5aeb-693b-7a8266722831"],
 " in units of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40b2cd92-d8d2-552c-7041-e4dfd9673c76"],
 ", which drops below one exactly when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "<", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d33a5f7-bec7-2be0-34c0-3cb13b7279ca"],
 ". Read ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4941c875-0f9b-4428-7f7e-e23faa2e2f72"],
 " off the same machinery:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1223896778,ExpressionUUID->"4eb25fa3-f83c-e31f-7642-560cf9cece65"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"zeroFreqSqueeze", "[", "\[CapitalOmega]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"mollowHom", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "0.", "}"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[403]:=",
 CellID->1594549589,ExpressionUUID->"62a92f6f-7b7e-c1b6-1256-c7497e08939c"],

Cell["and sweep it across the drive:", "Text",
 CellID->2059402855,ExpressionUUID->"7b95265a-e40c-d742-29aa-b8078dbebda8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"om", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"zeroFreqSqueeze", "[", "om", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"om", ",", " ", "0.05", ",", " ", "1.2", ",", " ", "0.02"}], 
      "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", "0.5", "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<drive \[CapitalOmega]/\[Gamma]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<zero-frequency spectrum S(0)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<the in-phase quadrature is squeezed only for \[CapitalOmega] < \
\[Gamma]/2\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[404]:=",
 CellID->1467764423,ExpressionUUID->"5dc2c791-5540-0ccd-0bf1-dedb5cf55617"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c7dbf89-8ebc-6f20-2402-36d32b49320a"],
 " dips below the shot-noise line on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "<", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2bac7c39-70bc-1c7f-5954-766301496745"],
 " (the vertical gridline) and rises above it past that drive, deepest at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"3", "-", 
     SqrtBox["7"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3295ea3d-90fd-c600-62aa-0c672089ad6a"],
 ", where it reaches ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"323", "-", "56", 
    SqrtBox["7"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "243"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "530a16a7-9aeb-8025-0109-8f011e9fd30f"],
 ". Push harder and the anti-squeezed quadrature's excess noise floods over \
the floor: the in-phase squeezing is a weak-drive effect, and the shallow \
spectral squeezing that lingers to higher drive has slid off zero frequency. \
Confirm the plotted curve is that closed form and not an artifact of the \
resolvent:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1197703646,ExpressionUUID->"6462a15f-fbd9-77bd-0c11-3918fe6c5d87"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"zeroFreqSqueeze", "[", "om", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"8", " ", 
         RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"4", " ", 
             RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"2", " ", 
              RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}]}]}], ")"}], "^", "3"}]}]}]}], ")"}]}], 
     "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"om", ",", " ", "0.05", ",", " ", "1.2", ",", " ", "0.05"}], 
     "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[405]:=",
 CellID->1917274169,ExpressionUUID->"35245787-1a09-692c-5cdc-4ee19fbc3876"],

Cell["\<\
The maximum discrepancy is at numerical precision. The whole spectroscopy, \
elastic line, inelastic triplet, and squeezing dip, comes from the two-time \
correlations of the same master equation built on the first page.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1680166544,ExpressionUUID->"0bd396c9-7dbe-c1cc-39e0-0f9374489316"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Where This Leaves Us", "Section",
 CellID->201557419,ExpressionUUID->"23367cc4-7482-6aab-52ce-75ae7d3738f1"],

Cell["\<\
From plain matrices and a few rules, we built a small laboratory for open \
quantum systems: the master equation for the unconditioned average, a \
positivity-preserving finite-step filter for a kept record, and plotters for \
the Bloch sphere, phase space, covariance ellipses, and spectra. On that \
base, twenty systems: pure dephasing, a driven damped atom, a cavity cat \
decohering at a rate set by the square of its separation, the Haroche \
experiment, dispersive qubit readout, quantum Brownian motion, the \
jump/homodyne/heterodyne unravellings, the quantum Zeno effect, a charge \
qubit read by a quantum point contact, measurement-induced collapse, a \
quantum Kalman filter, measurement feedback, thermalization, rapid \
purification, feedback cooling, the linear-vs-nonlinear trajectory, and the \
Mollow triplet. The recurring theme is conditionality: a complete ideal \
record can keep an initially pure state on a pure stochastic trajectory, \
whereas missed channels, inefficiency, or mixed initial data produce mixed \
conditional states. In every unravelling, ensemble recovery of the master \
equation is a joint large-sample and small-step limit. Change a number, rerun \
the convergence checks, and watch the physics move.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1708368016,ExpressionUUID->"302090d5-c821-dae1-61df-099ee9d5a8cb"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
},
